INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (2754, 'e7cfde8de9', '[quote:e7cfde8de9="DarkTari"]Hey C-Dub\r\n\r\nHaving a problem FTP\'ing files. I know it\'s something that I\'m not doing.\r\n\r\nI have Windows XP.  Got this from NOX:\r\n\r\nBut, I believe, and I can check with cabo.\r\nYou should have your own ftp area on lixlink.com.\r\nftp://darktari.lixlink.com/\r\nhttp://darktari.lixlink.com/   &lt;-- this didn\'t fail..so I think so.\r\n\r\njust need to get the password from cabo.\r\n\r\nfrom your file explorer or internet explorer, type in...\r\nftp://darktari:password@lixlink.com   (note the : (colon)  between your\r\nusername and password)\r\nthen click on sub-directory "Web"\r\nthen drag and drop any files you want into this window.\r\n\r\nfiles will be availabile to view on the web\r\nhttp://darktari.lixlink.com/filename.(html,jpg.gif,wmv,etc)\r\n\r\nIs this the proper proceedure.  I get to this directory but when I drag file, pic shows up on an MSN screen but not in directory. What am I doing wrong????\r\n\r\nThanx[/quote:e7cfde8de9]\r\nIt could be a limitation of the MSN browser, I\'m not sure, it should work if you are inside the "web" directory and drag a file into the browser window.\r\nI\'m guessing that your MSN browser is seeing you drag this file in to the the browser window and just thinks you want to open the file, so it does and you see the picture. In your address bar, you probably see the path to this file you see, on your hard drive.\r\n\r\nYou have a bunch of options as far as being able to FTP, it\'s just up to you to  pick which ever you feel is the easiest and makes you the most comfortable. Here\'s a few other options you can try, or if you don\'t like these options or have trouble with them, PM me back and we\'ll keep going till we get it working for you how you like it. (like Burger King or somethin) :lol: \r\n\r\n- Instead of using your MSN browser, use your Internet Explorer browser.\r\n- Instead of using your MSN browser, use an FTP program like CuteFTP, DreamWeaver, etc.\r\n- Instead of using your MSN browser, use DOS command prompt to FTP (this is by far the hardest way to ftp because everything is a manual and typed command, you have to know the commands to talk to the computer)\r\n\r\nlet me know how you fare and if you need help with anything or need other options or whatever - we can get you FTPing no doubt.');
