INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (4986, 'c8bf3894c2', 'i make bodykits out of the lexan packaging the bits come in ( you could use any type of clear plastic packaging). i use super glue to hold it together. i like to double up two pieces for stiffness. for the front of the car, i remove the body from the chassis, put it on the plastic, and trace the inside and the outside of front bumper on with a fine tip sharpie. create the design you want extending out from the outside outline on the plastic. [you might want to shave down the bottom lip of the bumper ( on the car ), paint it black, and throw a grill over it to make it look clean.when you put the new front lip on it will give it a custom, built in look.] oh yeah, do the tab lowering on the front of the chassis, it\'s a must do, and improves the look of the new body kit.\r\n     to install the front lip, cut it from the plastic and smooth the rough edges with sandpaper. put some super glue on the bottom of the bumper, and slap that custom lip on (straight, hopefully)and leave painting for the last step.\r\n     making sideskirts is pretty easy, snap the car back on the chassis, and grab for your handy dandy double-thick plastic, and sharpie.  put the plastic up against one side of the car, hold it a bit of the ground (for clearance) and draw a line for as high as you want it to sit on the side of the body. also trace the lines on the wheel wells, and continue them onto the portion of the sideskirt that hangs down. for the rear i just make little triangles that match the lines that the sideskirt produces. ( trace the sideskirts onto another portion of the plastic, so both sides are the exact same) cut them out, and glue them on the sides.\r\n     lastly paint your new bodykit to match the color of the car.\r\n\r\n     if you need any help, have questions, or are just totally confused about what i said in the last couple paragraphs, i\'d be glad to help a fellow pimp. :grin:');
