INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (7169, '0a0ecf7c87', 'I bought sheets of styrene from the LHS. They are .030 thick. I stacked 2 pieces together and cut them out the shape of the car, glued them on and trimmed.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (6546, '843a646e87', 'Hey Ahh, just one bit of advice.  The "B" pillar, none of the manufactures seem to paint it with the body. They leave it as part of the glass when it is clearly, to me at least, a part of the body and should be painted the body color. On my EVO, you can notice I painted the B &amp; rear door pillars. Tomy never paints these. Not trying to be a stickler cause your work is real good, just that final lil touch makes it look complete. Now if you tinted it I think it would look slick cause then it would look like it has no B pillar.\r\n[img:843a646e87]http://www.msnusers.com/_Secure/0PgCz*74RiBbL7n6bxGSO3sMA2nKzUwh6y4iDZH4jw7GYlpMnqbGqhs3N99Ln398wQspK0medILauAQuvixh8dL2Auq8sRGqf/EVO2.png?dc=4675431941286714948[/img:843a646e87]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (5716, 'cc40a7d8ca', '[quote:cc40a7d8ca="laanguiano"]What colors of paint could u do to make a fat car?  Or maybe those tight flame jobs ya do.\r\n\r\nWhat would i need to give ya for you to use your rx7?  And maybe make it a convert, or a drag looking car with lowered front.\r\n\r\nAlso, do bit bodys fit on thunder chargers?  \r\n\r\nLMK[/quote:cc40a7d8ca]The colors I have on hand are Medium Red Pearl(it\'s sorta a dark metallic red), Dark Blue (it\'s really dark like midnight blue), Gold, Charcoal, and Medium Charcoal. I don\'t have, but was planning to pick up, some blue, silver, and teal.\r\n\r\nI\'ll trade you the body straight across for the Homie, as long as you want colors I have, or was planning to get. I don\'t have to do flames, I do other graphics pretty good too. Oh, and of coarse give me credit for the paint when you show it off. ;)\r\n\r\nI don\'t lower the slot on the bodies anymore, I kept cracking too many bodies, so now I just lower the tab on the chassis. I\'ll try to find the thread at tinyRC where they show how to do that. \r\n\r\nI was actually planning to do a targa top, or a convertible on this body, but that takes a lot of time, and sliced fingers, I might have to ask for $$ if I did that.\r\n\r\nBit bodies don\'t fit directly on the Thunder Charger chassis, you have to do a little hacking.\r\nDave');
