INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12393, '063111b153', '[quote:063111b153="Swavey"]I am extending a bit to fit under custom casted resin body. Doing major modifications to the appearence of the chassis, but dual cell is to heavy for me. \r\n\r\nI have a plethera of shen pcb\'s lieing around, and a couple bit boosters, i would like to get the boosters set up with better speed, torque and steering. \r\n\r\nHow much you think that would cost?[/quote:063111b153]\r\n\r\nWell, here\'s a couple thoughts. My cost for FETS is $0.50 a piece, and I\'ve been selling sets of 4 for $4.00 shipped. Mailing a paded 6x9 envelope USPS costs just under $1.00.\r\n\r\nUsually I just mosfet forward and reverse, using 4 mosfets. Mosfetted steering is a rather negligible improvement. \r\n\r\nWhile it is easier to mail just a PCB, it\'s critical to be able to test the mosfet mod while doing it. To be able to do that, it needs to be in a chassis with a battery and motor. I suppose I have extra chassis with motors and batteries, but it adds quite a bit of time if I have to solder a PCB into a chassis, do the mod, and then unsolder the PCB to mail back. So, if you have a PCB in a chassis, it would be much easier on my end.\r\n\r\nHow many PCBs do you have laying around? I\'d be willing to trade my time for doing the mod for 49mhz PCBs, boosters if ya got em. Either way, I\'m gonna say my time to do the mod is worth $10-$20, and I\'m willing to trade for certain parts. Let me know what ya think.');
