INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (7448, '148faf3f2c', 'Thanks DT, I\'ve painted with and without primer. It seems like you don\'t have to pile on so much paint when you use primer. As for the pressure, that\'s where I am experimenting right now (in combination with the consitency of the paint). The Challenger used about a 3 parts paint to 2 parts thinner mixture and I shot it at about 12 psi. I just shot the first coat of color on my Camaro with a mixture of about 2 parts paint to 1 part thinner and shot it at about 18 psi and that\'s my best coat of paint yet. They both worked well, and I will probably shoot for something between the two for the next one.\r\n\r\nIn general, I think the least amout of pressure that still gives a good flow, then getting in there pretty tight (I shoot at about 1.5 to 2 inches from the car), and keep moving. Right when it looks wet and glossy, stop. The trick is bringing the whole car to that point gradually instead of working one spot at a time (what will happen is those parts will dry a bit and any overspray will cause a textured look)\r\n\r\nI\'m still figuring it out, but that\'s where I am for now.');
