INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (8120, '42ee484a64', '[quote:42ee484a64]I doubt I could do the Nakamichi, pretty sure they have a different PCB, and I\'m not good at figuring out circuits, I\'m just good at following instructions.\r\n\r\nAs for the details, The Thunder Charger has a PCB from an original Microsizer, and the Zip Zap has your Cyclona PCB, but I was thinking maybe I should switch them around so you can use a Zip Zap controller w/ the Zip Zap, since the MS board is 27mhz. What do you think about that?\r\n\r\nIf you ever want me to do any more mosfet mods I would be happy to do them for more mosfets. I\'m addicted to them suckers now, and really want some more! I was thinking about pimpin\' my mosfet mods at BitPimps, so I could hustle up some more mosfets, but I decided to wait until you get your cars, so you can vouch for my work.\r\n\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:42ee484a64]\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ll open up one of the Naks and take some pics....I have a camcorder I usually use....but my Mutha-in-law has a digi-cam....I\'ll take some really clear pics and show you...we\'ll see whatcha think...cool? and if not....maybe throw Cyclona or MS pcbs into them ? \r\n\r\nI would like to use the ZZ controller if you really feel like doing it....it would help me distinguish between the 2 at race time and the ZZ controller is more comfy......if you want...if not, no biggie....\r\n\r\nMy only regret about giving you props on the mods will be the fact that I cannot download video to show everyone here.....if you want to video the cars in action...we could collaborate and post it for everyone to see.....if you want of course....I figure the video could speak for itself......and I\'m sure it would get you some mosfet mod business if you wanted it......');
