INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11260, 'a536f8edfd', '[quote:a536f8edfd="TeamBonzer"]HI CW\r\n\r\njust saw your picture of the green 350z - very coool.\r\n\r\nCan I put it on my site, with link to bitpimp home page (or wherever you want someone to go who wants to see more custom jobs?)\r\n\r\nI\'ll credit you as CW unless you want something else?\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nDerek[/quote:a536f8edfd]hey bonzer,\r\nthanks for the props and thanks for asking.\r\nI have to ask that you please not use it though.\r\nI\'ve had to turn other people/sites down in the past, so I have to do the same here or I\'ll create a huge mess for myself.\r\nWe get a very large amount of requests for people wanting to use our images, and it puts us in a very tight spot.\r\n\r\nthanks again for checking with me first, I appreciate that tremendously!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11248, '4bf8943d19', 'Well I do have a LXX that I ripped apart and all is left is the chassie and board.  As for internal duel cells, I am not good with cells I fried a bunch already tring to solder them together and just gave up on them for now.  I am getting some external duel cell cars from hog but as for the internal not sure about that one yet lol  damn cells and heat');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11730, 'd024d6315d', 'Cool\r\n\r\n  I will toss a 4.2 Pro (blue endbell) in the package :)\r\n\r\n  Tell me what you think of the motor if you car is mosfeted then forget about it LOL it just alittle blur whippin around the track/floor lol\r\n\r\n But I find it still gots some good torque even with the teal gears');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11732, '0713730b45', 'Awesome dood.... Thanks a million... I can\'t wait now... I\'ll be like a friggin kid on Christmas.......lol\r\n\r\n\r\n-S');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11251, 'a26129912c', 'how do I flush my flash/shockwave cache?\r\n\r\nI still hear the old playlist. I have done the following\r\n\r\nUpgraded to DW and Flash 2004.\r\nCleared all temp dir complteley.\r\nTried before logging in.\r\nrebooted numerous times\r\n\r\n&gt;&gt;?????&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11299, '5ae8232bd7', 'ok, I want you to do a mosfet for me on an LXX booster. But seeing that I am in Barbados and have access to nothing, I would like to know if you have any other things lying around.\r\n\r\nLike:\r\nA couple sheets of decal paper\r\nand maybe some modeling putty\r\nand the small batteries for the internl dual/tri cell  (button cells)\r\n\r\nIf you want some more money for those things we can negotiate :cool: \r\nBut i mainly want the mosfet\r\n\r\nThank you');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11253, '18cf789bf2', '[quote:18cf789bf2="VooDooMafia"]Well I do have a LXX that I ripped apart and all is left is the chassie and board.  As for internal duel cells, I am not good with cells I fried a bunch already tring to solder them together and just gave up on them for now.  I am getting some external duel cell cars from hog but as for the internal not sure about that one yet lol  damn cells and heat[/quote:18cf789bf2]\r\n\r\nI got a few extra batteries, I\'ll throw a 2nd cell in there if you want me to.  A dual cell mosfet modded ZZ is crazy fun.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11254, '4da1614f4e', '[quote:4da1614f4e="TeamBonzer"]Didnt mean to piss you off so much. Didnt mean to piss you off at all!. \r\n\r\nI\'ve only had 32 entries to the comp, so I guess that the odds are better than the lottery, and I kinda hoped that a pimp would win - hence the post. \r\n\r\nYou been good to me, and the board has helped me keep the faith (as in living the dream), that I appreciate - thanks. So Im sorry if you got the wrong slant on my post, didnt mean to offend.\r\n\r\nHey, and I always post here first :D \r\n\r\nTook me a long time to phrase this because I care  :| \r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTeamBonzer[/quote:4da1614f4e]No worries homie. Now we both know where we\'re coming from. I didn\'t mean to come off too harshly, guess I let part of my mood come across in the forums.\r\nI did want you to know you are free to keep making those type of posts, just please use an existing thread to keep us updated on that stuff.\r\n\r\n...and I thank you very much for being appreciative and understanding...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11255, 'dbfc69763c', 'Ok here\'s the breakdown of what\'s up with the rims.\r\n\r\nThe WT4343 should be no problem. Those are cool, because they are so narrow.\r\n\r\nThe WT4379. Those should be easie than normal to mount. They have smaller holes, and I wont need my pen tips, but I don\'t know if the the little center piece will fit over the front pin when mounted. I might have to glue the piece to the pin, so it stays stationary while the wheel spins. These wheels have water slide decals. I hope i don\'t mess those up, i haven\'t touched a water slide decal since I was kid.\r\n\r\nThe WT4314, ok now here\'s where I\'ve got a real issue. You sent me a mismatched set. I have four large tires, 2 smaller wider tires. 2 of the smaller wider rims already assembled, and 3 large rings, and 2 large backs. (see pic)\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if you have the other pieces or not so here\'s the options, either you could send me the missing pieces so I can complete the set of 4314s, or I could put the 2 smaller ones in front, the large ones in back. Do a bit of \'fabricating\' to narrow the front to the same width as the back, and trim the gold 6 spoke pieces to fit in the smaller rims in the front so they match with the back.\r\n\r\nAlso which rims do you want on the Zip Zap?\r\n\r\ndave\r\n[img:dbfc69763c]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/havoks.jpg[/img:dbfc69763c]');
