INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12276, '71723fa154', '[quote:71723fa154="crazydave"]Oh ok, I guess I didn\'t pay that close attention to your post, sorry man. I feel silly now. I guess I was just hung up on mAs. \r\n\r\nYeah I can get voltage readings. I\'ll be doing some modding tomorrow, I\'ll get to it then, and post my findings. \r\n\r\n...and yeah Nox will hook you up. I\'ve delt with him.\r\n\r\nI just didn\'t know if you needed a hook up or not since you\'re still waiting, but if you do I\'m always willing to help a pimp out.\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:71723fa154]\r\n\r\nThat\'s cool man about the readings, no sweats, no biggie, lol.\r\n\r\n(sorry -VE means negative/ground, +VE mean the positive voltage rail, battery terminal, etc...GND means ground/negative, sorry dude, did a ee degree so I talk short techowise, :) )\r\n\r\nWith your MM put the -VE probe on the gnd rail or -ve battery terminal, if you can clip it there it makes taking readings easier.   Remove the motor from the circuit so the two terminals on the pcb aren\'t taking a load.\r\n\r\nWith no signal on the circuit, take the voltage reading from the two motor solder pads on the PCB, record these values in the table.\r\n\r\nNow put the controller at full throttle fwd, take the readings again for Voltage, record them.\r\n\r\nNow put the controller at full throttle in rev, again take the readings and record.\r\n\r\nThe reason to this methodical madness is to see what the voltage does on these pins.  If we can\'t increase the output signal from the chip (as micro states as being fixed at 0.9V) then we have to look at alternative ways of amplifying that signal.  The downfall of this investigation is that the end product might result in a seperate "piggy backed" circuit.  We\'ll see.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nmatt.');
