INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11657, '5dc63c6044', '[quote:5dc63c6044="VooDooMafia"]OK cool\r\n\r\n  And let me know when you are gonna make another fet order and if you are gonna be doing more cars :)\r\n\r\n  I have cars that are gonna be upset with the lack of use till they get fetted up lol.\r\n\r\n  I know that mini z and suck can be fetted, but can any RC be fetted(micro that is)?\r\n\r\n   I only ask cause I picked up a mini sub to casue shit at the local pet shop(my buddy runs the reptile section and hates the fish guy), and think its nnot gonna be fast enough to keep up with thems fish lol\r\n\r\nPete[/quote:5dc63c6044]Almost any RC should use transistors that can be replaced with mosfets. The thing is sometimes due to other issues on the circuit, FETs might not always help.\r\n\r\nThe other issue is if there are PNP transistors, I have to flip the FET, and figure where to put hat third jumper.\r\n\r\nI\'m sure it can be done, but I\'d have to work at it.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (11579, 'f3d3f1500a', '[quote:f3d3f1500a="VooDooMafia"]I am not sure what the frequency is as these LXX used numbers as there was a set of 4 cars.\r\n\r\n  So they were 01,02,03 &amp; 04.\r\n\r\n  Ok I figureed I would test it before I sent this.  The LXX seems to be 49mHz as I charged the Zip up and used the LXX controller to run it.\r\n\r\n  The only thing is when you press forward it went backward and same with steering.\r\n\r\n  You want me send the Zip controller aswell?\r\n\r\n  Oh and I will say this now but Sorry for the coins :?[/quote:f3d3f1500a]Yeah I just swap the wires around. \r\n\r\nI take the PCB out when I do the mosfet mod, so I don\'t have to worry about breaking your steering wires and sending you back a car with mended steering wires. \r\n\r\nSo I have to wire it all back up anyways, that\'s why I offered you the option of what controller you wanted to use.\r\n\r\nI have all the ZZ controllers, so you don\'t need to send any of those.\r\n\r\nCoins are cool, need them to fill up my water jugs. :grin: \r\n\r\nDave');
