INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12175, '9ba4d0dcbe', '[quote:9ba4d0dcbe="MadScott"]CW, just wanted to give you the heads up that this guy is using stuff from over here and probably not giving y\'all much credit for it.  Also wanted to share a recent email that I sent him.  He\'s been a pest over at MRCC and made it sound like he was dissing you guys with no regard.\r\n\r\n[quote:9ba4d0dcbe]Thank you Scott, yeah the whole thing took us by surprise, since we \r\ngive \r\nmad links to the sources everywhere, and don\'t copy the whole tutorials \r\njust link directly to them. Now ZipZaps.com, we copied the tutorials \r\nbecause A) official company and B) they had these microcosmic windows \r\nthat \r\nwere hard to use.\r\n\r\nThe images, we just copied and put them right next to the same title as \r\nthe \r\npage they linked to and even said "(at the BitPimps website)" and \r\nlinked \r\ndirectly to the index of the site, not just the article, in the word \r\nBitPimps. This is no more than Google News does every day. And why go \r\nthrough the trouble of copying those images? Usability. People like to \r\nknow \r\nwhat they are clicking on before they click on a link, and a picture \r\nspeaks \r\na thousand words. We never thought we\'d make people mad but as Marty \r\npointed out... you make some people mad by breathing.\r\n\r\nAt this point, any energy we spend talking to these people will just \r\nmake \r\nthem more mad because they\'ve already made up their minds, so our only \r\nreal \r\noption is to just ignore it. [b:9ba4d0dcbe]BitPimps, for all their fluster, has not \r\nbothered to actually send us an e-mail so we assume that that\'s all \r\nthey \r\nhave at the moment... fluster.[/b:9ba4d0dcbe]\r\n\r\nI\'m David, but me and three other guys put this together. See our About \r\npage.\r\n\r\nAs for blogging, hah hah... the buck stops there. There is no way you \r\ncan \r\navoid having people link to whatever the heck they want. It is common \r\nlaw \r\namong webmasters not to directly link to files or images, but webpages? \r\nGive me a break.\r\n\r\nThanks for your time, Scott.  I\'ll be leet-speaking when next you see \r\nme, \r\nprobably ;)\r\n\r\nAt 10:43 AM 10/17/2003, you wrote:\r\n\r\n&gt;DavidBeoulve,\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;MadScott has sent you this email from \r\n&gt;http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/index.php.\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;Please take a moment to read through our forum guidelines found here, \r\n&gt;http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/index.php?act=boardrules.  Just to \r\ngive \r\n&gt;you a heads up, you are starting to get a few folks at MRCC mad by \r\nusing \r\n&gt;images without their permission.  You may want to email or PM folks \r\nbefore \r\n&gt;you decide to blog or use their images.  Just trying to help you out \r\nhere.\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;Thanks,\r\n&gt;Madscott\r\n[/quote:9ba4d0dcbe]\r\nLike I said, more than anything I just wanted to give you guys the heads up because he\'s starting to piss off guys like ph2t.  Thanks for the time man.\r\n\r\nMadScott[/quote:9ba4d0dcbe]thanks for the heads up.\r\nI have contact him via e-mail, I\'ve contact his host, and I\'ve contact his hosts\' provider and I\'ve contact their providers\' provider.\r\nSo, I contacted David, I contacted Geof (owner of the domain), I contact his host (iPowerWeb) and I contacted their provider (AT&amp;T).\r\n\r\nHis site should be shut down soon.\r\n\r\nthanks again for the heads up, I might just have to make a trip over the MRCC just to put this dude in his place.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12184, '8b51a57138', '[quote:8b51a57138="CaboWabo"][quote:8b51a57138="ph2t"][quote:8b51a57138="CaboWabo"]houston, we\'ve got problems lol\r\n\r\nI swapped out the motor tonite, put a little charge in it and turned on the car... nothing.\r\nrepositioned the motor, nothing.\r\n\r\nput the other motor back in, charged it a bit, nothing.\r\n\r\nI think that switch may be where my current is breaking?\r\nhows the switch attached to the chassis? will I be able to pull off the switch and remount it?[/quote:8b51a57138]\r\n\r\nawww shit, I hate this!   i tested it fully before shipping back, arghhhh!\r\n\r\nNow that rant n rave is done let\'s see what I can do.\r\n\r\nwhen you charge it and turn it on do the lights work? or this there absolutely nothing?  Also try leaving the switch in the ON position and then charging.   Does the motor and lights work this way?\r\n\r\nThe switch is glued to the chassis, prying out off might work.  One wire goes to the metal battery tab at the bottom of the chassis, so the wire sorta travels under the battery if ya get my drift.   The other wire goes straight to the +V terminal on the pcb.\r\n\r\nAlso check to make sure that the metal points the charger touches are funny visible from the underside fo the chassis.\r\n\r\nHere\'s tome hints, I\'ll await feedback.   God I hope it\'s not fuck, that would really suck.  If it gets to that Ill pay shipping back to fix....if it gets to that :sad: \r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:8b51a57138]aight, it\'s not the switch.\r\nI fudged around with it more last night.\r\nI ended up re-positioning the battery inside the chassis and it came back on. If I pushed the battery too firmly in to position, it would cut the current and the lights and car would turn back off.\r\nSo I think it\'s the wire that runs under that battery, for sure fixable - so I wouldn\'t worry. I think all I gotta do is find the sweet spot for that wire and alls good.\r\n\r\nthanks for the help bro![/quote:8b51a57138]\r\n\r\nfhew!   I\'m happy to hear that.   Dang man sorry for the troubles....Kick my arse, lol!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
