INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12215, '51f50bddd5', '[quote:51f50bddd5="ph2t"][quote:51f50bddd5="CaboWabo"][quote:51f50bddd5="ph2t"][quote:51f50bddd5="CaboWabo"]houston, we\'ve got problems lol\r\n\r\nI swapped out the motor tonite, put a little charge in it and turned on the car... nothing.\r\nrepositioned the motor, nothing.\r\n\r\nput the other motor back in, charged it a bit, nothing.\r\n\r\nI think that switch may be where my current is breaking?\r\nhows the switch attached to the chassis? will I be able to pull off the switch and remount it?[/quote:51f50bddd5]\r\n\r\nawww shit, I hate this!   i tested it fully before shipping back, arghhhh!\r\n\r\nNow that rant n rave is done let\'s see what I can do.\r\n\r\nwhen you charge it and turn it on do the lights work? or this there absolutely nothing?  Also try leaving the switch in the ON position and then charging.   Does the motor and lights work this way?\r\n\r\nThe switch is glued to the chassis, prying out off might work.  One wire goes to the metal battery tab at the bottom of the chassis, so the wire sorta travels under the battery if ya get my drift.   The other wire goes straight to the +V terminal on the pcb.\r\n\r\nAlso check to make sure that the metal points the charger touches are funny visible from the underside fo the chassis.\r\n\r\nHere\'s tome hints, I\'ll await feedback.   God I hope it\'s not fuck, that would really suck.  If it gets to that Ill pay shipping back to fix....if it gets to that :sad: \r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:51f50bddd5]aight, it\'s not the switch.\r\nI fudged around with it more last night.\r\nI ended up re-positioning the battery inside the chassis and it came back on. If I pushed the battery too firmly in to position, it would cut the current and the lights and car would turn back off.\r\nSo I think it\'s the wire that runs under that battery, for sure fixable - so I wouldn\'t worry. I think all I gotta do is find the sweet spot for that wire and alls good.\r\n\r\nthanks for the help bro![/quote:51f50bddd5]\r\n\r\nfhew!   I\'m happy to hear that.   Dang man sorry for the troubles....Kick my arse, lol!\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:51f50bddd5]dude, don\'t even sweat it - I\'m not the typical kiddie - I know how this shit works.\r\nyou did fine, I\'m still please, just gotta find a better position for the wire contacts... whatever, I\'m not even sure there is a better spot yet so seriously, don\'t sweat it bro.');
