INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12232, '7aa210634c', 'hey man, I emailed micro last night to get him to spill his guts and I got this email back:\r\n\r\n[quote:7aa210634c]\r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: Roland \r\nTo: ph2t \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:41 PM\r\nSubject: Shhh, secret\r\n\r\n\r\nHehehe, Matt I think I might keep my cards close to my chest on this one for a little while yet.\r\nI only just got it all together today.\r\nI want to let the news get out there first, I\'m hoping to pick up a few mods out of this as well.\r\nAll will be revealed, but not straight away.\r\nSorry man, dont mean to be a prick, I\'d just like to get a little bit back from this one because I\'ve put a few hours into it to get to this point, and I am hoping to see some kind of return.\r\nCheers, \r\nRoland\r\n\r\n\r\n. \r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: ph2t \r\nTo: Roland \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:26 PM\r\nSubject: spill yer guts.....\r\n\r\n\r\nso how did you do the mod yer smart bugger?  c\'mon spill!\r\n\r\nDid you use another switching transistor?   Increase the voltage on the controller chip power rail?  ???\r\n\r\nthanks man,\r\n\r\nMatt.\r\n[/quote:7aa210634c]\r\n\r\nSo you can see he ain\'t gonna release this mod soon publicly.  bugger.   From a development point of view though I\'m happy to keep working with you to get a solution going.   This would be publicly available of course.  Your call man, I\'ve put the offer up but I need someone that has a zzse to do the goundwork with me, until I get mine of course, lol.   Tell me to bugger off and leave you alone otherwise.:)\r\n\r\ncheers Dave,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12233, '7aa210634c', 'hey man, I emailed micro last night to get him to spill his guts and I got this email back:\r\n\r\n[quote:7aa210634c]\r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: Roland \r\nTo: ph2t \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:41 PM\r\nSubject: Shhh, secret\r\n\r\n\r\nHehehe, Matt I think I might keep my cards close to my chest on this one for a little while yet.\r\nI only just got it all together today.\r\nI want to let the news get out there first, I\'m hoping to pick up a few mods out of this as well.\r\nAll will be revealed, but not straight away.\r\nSorry man, dont mean to be a prick, I\'d just like to get a little bit back from this one because I\'ve put a few hours into it to get to this point, and I am hoping to see some kind of return.\r\nCheers, \r\nRoland\r\n\r\n\r\n. \r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: ph2t \r\nTo: Roland \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:26 PM\r\nSubject: spill yer guts.....\r\n\r\n\r\nso how did you do the mod yer smart bugger?  c\'mon spill!\r\n\r\nDid you use another switching transistor?   Increase the voltage on the controller chip power rail?  ???\r\n\r\nthanks man,\r\n\r\nMatt.\r\n[/quote:7aa210634c]\r\n\r\nSo you can see he ain\'t gonna release this mod soon publicly.  bugger.   From a development point of view though I\'m happy to keep working with you to get a solution going.   This would be publicly available of course.  Your call man, I\'ve put the offer up but I need someone that has a zzse to do the goundwork with me, until I get mine of course, lol.   Tell me to bugger off and leave you alone otherwise.:)\r\n\r\ncheers Dave,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12740, '5aa22ce566', '[quote:5aa22ce566="crazydave"]Got the Excel spread sheet updated, and uploaded.\r\n\r\nDisregard my last numbers, these ones are garanteed accurate, because I had an extra pair of hands helping this time.\r\n\r\nThe voltage is lower because I ran the car for few before I tested. the battery had a starting voltage of 2.73. Notice forward drops in voltage more than reverse. That\'s because the FETs are stacked in forward.\r\n\r\nMaybe you can explain this system to me. I would have thought one of the wires would be ground, and read 0. It seems to be a system of balance, but I don\'t get it. :? \r\n\r\nAs you upside down people say, cheers,\r\nDave[/quote:5aa22ce566]\r\n\r\nThanks again mate for the info.  I\'ll have a  look and the sheet and pics today. :)\r\n\r\nHere\'s an email I got from Micro in response to some questions I sent him. Hope this "enlightens" you.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\nMatt.\r\n\r\n---------- Original Message ----------------------------------\r\nFrom: "Roland" &lt;rolands@dodo.com.au&gt;\r\nDate:  Mon, 27 Oct 2003 09:44:30 +1100\r\n\r\n&gt;Hmmm, sounds a bit strange.\r\n&gt;my wire colours were a bit different.\r\n&gt;not sure on the 3rd wire though, the steering motor wires are right next to\r\n&gt;the drive motor terminals and I think he may have taken readings from this\r\n&gt;one as well (??)\r\n&gt;The ZZ SE has a data line terminal as well (a third pin) under the car, that\r\n&gt;is what reprograms the \'channel\' when you charge it up.\r\n&gt;Maybe he has taken readings off this as well, who knows.\r\n&gt;There is also a yellow wire on the steering feedback pot, (this is the only\r\n&gt;yellow on mine)\r\n&gt;(You really need to wait until you get your cars to work through it,\r\n&gt;emailing this kind of stuff back and forth (especially with someone who is\r\n&gt;not 100% techo) can be a pain, let me tell you.)\r\n&gt;Goodluck.\r\n&gt;Roland\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;.\r\n&gt;----- Original Message -----\r\n&gt;From: "ph2t" &lt;ph2t@prahranpianos.com&gt;\r\n&gt;To: &lt;rolands@dodo.com.au&gt;\r\n&gt;Sent: Monday, October 27, 2003 9:23 AM\r\n&gt;Subject: hey\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt; hey man. Just a question with guess what? the SE\'s, lol....\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt; There are three wires going to the drive motor.  Do you know what these\r\n&gt;are for.   Here\'s some readings that were taken by crazydave and he asked me\r\n&gt;why there would be three wires.   To me it looks like only two are being\r\n&gt;used as the drive voltages, wires yellow and grey.   Your comments man?\r\n&gt;Where do these wires go?  I will have my zzse in about a week, yeah!   See\r\n&gt;the attached s/sheet.\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt; Thanks dude,\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt; Matt.\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;&gt;\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt;');
