INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12252, '8bfba67c89', '[quote:8bfba67c89]  Well I bought another se off of ez so that one will want to get fetted later aswell :)\r\n\r\n  Yea I am sure he will post something eventually but I will keep looking on the msg boards and shit.\r\n\r\n  Aso I was gonna msg him and ask him what he had to do to get it all working good.  Considering he knows that I know shit about the electronics of them really he might just tell me to be cockey and sound really smart(not to say hes not).\r\n\r\n  As for the Mat car I will package one up.  I had to have 2 myself, 1 for the collection and one to mod(fet,paint,wheels).  I did use the rims on the truck I did it looks ok with them(only in a pic at ausmicro).[/quote:8bfba67c89]Cool thanks for the MAT car. I appreciate it.  :grin: \r\n\r\nNow I think that leaves you one up on me. If there\'s anything else I could do, let me know. ;)\r\n\r\nMaybe some charcoal flames fading in on the Beetle body?\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12253, '57af6d0c54', 'Sup Pimp!\r\n\r\nYou have been gone a while.  The body modding material is called Styrene.\r\nI use 0.60 for the ground effects, and 0.30 &amp; 0.20 for various other mods.\r\nYou can usually find it at your LHS or you can order it from here....\r\n\r\nhttp://www.micromark.com/\r\n\r\n[i:57af6d0c54]These plastic sheets can be used for fabricating model structures, car bodies, airplane cowls, dollhouse and miniature furniture \'glass,\' windshields and other window glazing. Easily glued, they can also be vacuum formed to create specialized [/i:57af6d0c54]shapes.\r\n \r\n[b:57af6d0c54]Butyrate:[/b:57af6d0c54] Optically clear, easily cut, dimensionally stable. Great for model window glazing. \r\n \r\n[b:57af6d0c54]Styrene:[/b:57af6d0c54] Multipurpose high-strength opaque plastic. Excellent for structure walls and roofs.\r\n\r\n[b:57af6d0c54]Vivak:[/b:57af6d0c54] Multipurpose high-strength clear plastic. Use for forming airplane canopies.\r\n\r\n[b:57af6d0c54]Polycarbonate:[/b:57af6d0c54] An unbreakable, high-temperature plastic. Ideal for forming engine cowls');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (13043, 'ea4ffc8047', '[quote:ea4ffc8047="VooDooMafia"]Sorry to hear about the wife, she have plans on were to look for work or something lined up?\r\n\r\n  By chance did you end up posting a car on ebay?\r\n\r\n  As for the package going out thanks but there was no rush, I got my bithed order today with some cool shit in it like the super bit speed sets with gold bling rims(front and back).\r\n\r\n\r\n  well if I can help in anyway let me know I can see what I can do :)[/quote:ea4ffc8047]Yeah she\'s got a couple leads, and while she\'s out of work, we\'re getting some goverment assistance, food stamps, access, WIC and all that stuff, plus she\'s getting her 2 weeks vacation time in cash. So if we can just get her right back to work we\'ll actually come out a ahead, and it might be a good thing. I just wish she at least lined something up first, I hate not having a plan for next week, but I\'m getting an XMod next payday, no matter what. That way if she never gets a job, and we end up homeless, I\'ll at least have an XMod.  :lol: \r\n\r\n...and yeah I know you said no hurry, but you know I say that sometimes too, we never [i:ea4ffc8047]really[/i:ea4ffc8047] mean it. Besides the longer I put it off the harder it would be to do. I hate riding the bus.\r\n\r\nI\'m going to post a couple cars this weekened. What I\'m actually gonna do is stretch a Thunder Charger chassis to fit Zip Zap bodies, paint the body up, dual cell it, and mosfet mod it. I figure the more work I put into it, with minimal investment, the more profit I make, per car, and that way I don\'t have to deal with as many people. Does that make any sense?\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12793, '2935468012', '[quote:2935468012="VooDooMafia"]Not sure what the laws are on the spray pants but I think I saw that stuff there aswell.  But I am just gonna pick up the duplicolor clearcoat as I think it was due to mixing the paints.  As soon the the clearcoat hit the paint it cracked and I let the duplicolor sit for 2 days before doing anything to it cause I was busy on other projects.\r\n\r\n  Lesson learned I guess lol but yea I figured I can\'t go wrong with the same brand.\r\n\r\n BTW our walmarts here suck lol the one walmart in town has about 25 different colors and the other about 5.  Will prolly take a trip to the auto store as they will have a better selection.[/quote:2935468012]Yep,you let it sit too long. The laquer will soften the paint, and plastic below, more so the plastic. That what makes it bubble and lift. It cracks because it expands when it lifts. So you want to recoat while it\'s fresh so the paint melts together, and that\'s also how you get a good bond that wont chip. Also lay a few light mister coats  before you lay any heavy coats, and that will keep the clear from mixing wth the color coats below.\r\n\r\n...and yeah I\'d look at the auto parts store. My Walmart only has about 20 colors too, but Checker auto has a whole aisle with countless colors. I only get it at walmart because it\'s a buck cheaper there.\r\n\r\nDave\r\n\r\nI just get them from Walmart because they\'re about a buck cheaper.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12273, 'e4d1b11339', 'Ahh5hit,\r\n\r\nCongratulations,  Your Skyline has been chosen as this weeks \r\n"Ride of Da Week"');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12257, 'bbd508a7b8', '[quote:bbd508a7b8="ph2t"]hey man, I emailed micro last night to get him to spill his guts and I got this email back:\r\n\r\n[quote:bbd508a7b8]\r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: Roland \r\nTo: ph2t \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:41 PM\r\nSubject: Shhh, secret\r\n\r\n\r\nHehehe, Matt I think I might keep my cards close to my chest on this one for a little while yet.\r\nI only just got it all together today.\r\nI want to let the news get out there first, I\'m hoping to pick up a few mods out of this as well.\r\nAll will be revealed, but not straight away.\r\nSorry man, dont mean to be a prick, I\'d just like to get a little bit back from this one because I\'ve put a few hours into it to get to this point, and I am hoping to see some kind of return.\r\nCheers, \r\nRoland\r\n\r\n\r\n. \r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: ph2t \r\nTo: Roland \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:26 PM\r\nSubject: spill yer guts.....\r\n\r\n\r\nso how did you do the mod yer smart bugger?  c\'mon spill!\r\n\r\nDid you use another switching transistor?   Increase the voltage on the controller chip power rail?  ???\r\n\r\nthanks man,\r\n\r\nMatt.\r\n[/quote:bbd508a7b8]\r\n\r\nSo you can see he ain\'t gonna release this mod soon publicly.  bugger.   From a development point of view though I\'m happy to keep working with you to get a solution going.   This would be publicly available of course.  Your call man, I\'ve put the offer up but I need someone that has a zzse to do the goundwork with me, until I get mine of course, lol.   Tell me to bugger off and leave you alone otherwise.:)\r\n\r\ncheers Dave,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:bbd508a7b8]Hey man, thank for the heads up.\r\n\r\nYeah I didn\'t think he\'d spill the beans right off the bat. We\'ll have to work at him for some hints. \r\n\r\nI\'d love to help you in any way I can. I\'d love for this knowledge to be made public. No offense to micro_Amps, he\'s cool, and I don\'t mean to cut into his business in any way, but I think it\'s just way too expensive for us American pimps to send our cars to the other side of the world to be FET\'ed. I mean they are just toys, don\'t want to get too carried away. I like to keep a little levity on my obcessions.\r\n\r\nI saw that you were asking for some reading. I have a problem wih that. I have a cheap multi-meter, and for some reason it\'s range is up to 200mA, the it\'s next setting up is 1A. So I made a mistake buying that meter, I need one that reads up to 500 or 1000mA.\r\n\r\nSo I can\'t help you there, but if you have any crazy theories you want me to try out, I\'ll try to help as best as I can. :grin: \r\n\r\nHey you know my local Shack has the SE, if you need someone to score one for you, just let me know. I\'m tight on money these days, so you\'d have to pay up front, but you could use Paypal, you know, that way you could be an ass and take your money back, but I know you wouldn\'t do that.;)\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12258, '1fdd5dac9e', '[quote:1fdd5dac9e="VooDooMafia"]Yo you are never on MSN hehe\r\n\r\n  hey you know the fet fix from micro amps?[/quote:1fdd5dac9e]\r\n\r\nhey man, yeah I\'ve been living at work the last week, massive network migrations, it sucks.\r\n\r\nDo you mean the zz se fet fix?  If so then no, he hasn\'t told me :(\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12783, '9516567f9e', '[quote:9516567f9e="VooDooMafia"]Hey Dave I had a Q for yea cause I know you are the dupli-color man lol\r\n\r\n  I picked up some cans of dupli-color enamel paint, but what clear coat should be used with it?\r\n\r\n  I used the same clearcoat I was using with the testersenamels I have but it made the paint crack when I sprayed it on my newly detailed bug Grrrrr.\r\n\r\n  Its prolly my clearcoat I was was cheap and just used the "Motomaster" canadian Tire car clearcoat for cars/trucks.\r\n\r\n  Man that sucks, oh well gives me a chance to sand out some of the imperfections I found after laying the paint on.[/quote:9516567f9e]That is so ironic. I was just telling Bilbobaggins to be careful because he used some Krylon enamel over the Duplicolor which is laquer. I was just telling him to be careful for that very reason. \r\n\r\nYou should check into that thread and back me up on what could happen.\r\n\r\nAnyways, the absolute safest, most fail proof way to go is with Duplicolor clear coat. It\'s good to stick to the same brand, but Plasti-cote also makes automotive laquers, and they have this stuff that is super duper shiny, and blingy, called Candy Apple/Metal Flake clear. I\'ve had some issues with that stuff bubbling in the crevices when I lay the coats too heavy over the Duplicolor, but if your careful the results are worth it.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12316, 'e8310dcd94', '[quote:e8310dcd94="crazydave"]You know I\'m not really a complainer, but there is bit of an issue going on behind the scenes. I hope I\'m not out of line bringing this up.\r\n\r\nSee Micro_amps has cracked the issue with SE, but is refusing to share his info. That is to be expected, he\'s a business man, like I\'ve been telling everyone, and people are starting to see it.\r\n\r\nSo anyways, yesterday me, ph2t, and VDM had been PMing each other about it. ph2t sent me copy of the email where micro_amps declared that he intended to get something out of this, because he put a few hours into it. \r\n\r\nMe and ph2t are working together to come up with our own solution. We want our info to be made public, ph2t because of creative development. Me because I think it\'s ridiculous to send your car to the other side of the world, end up paying 50 bucks just to have 2 dollars worth of mosfets installed in your car. It takes me about 20-30 minutes nowadays. I feel micro_amps is ripping people off, and I don\'t dig on that.\r\n\r\nAnyways, here\'s where you come in. I not sure if you would consider this spamming, but micro_amps just posted this thread annoucing he\'s open for business on the SE mods. I personally felt this was crass self promotion, but it\'s your site your call, i just wanted to bring to your attention what went down yesterday.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2317\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:e8310dcd94]excellent.\r\nyes for sure bring stuff like this up to my attention.\r\nI had no clue, I never really looked at microAmps that way but taking just a few seconds to look from another perspective, I can see where you could come up with that.\r\n\r\nI agree, it\'s bogus, which is the exact reason why I\'ve never had him do anything for me. I\'ve tried out just about all the others that I have interest in dealing with, all went great. still leary on microAmps though.\r\n\r\nI know for sure the dude knows what he is doing when it comes to electronics, so that\'s where my curiousity lies. but I\'m not so curious that I\'m going to help make the guy rich. I know how much that shits costing him and probably a good guess on time, he\'s raking it in for what he\'s doing. The knowledge sharing thing, that just makes me mad and makes him look kinda like the chump he must be if he\'s willing to do things like that.\r\n\r\nI\'ll let the other moderators know about the gist of it and we\'ll all decide what the best way to handle this is.\r\n\r\nthanks again and don\'t worry, you\'re not out of line.\r\nyou see an issue that may turn into a huge problem, I\'m glad there are people who can recognize these things and bring them to someones attention so there\'s a chance for a remedy.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12261, '286611e739', '[quote:286611e739="crazydave"][quote:286611e739="ph2t"]hey man, I emailed micro last night to get him to spill his guts and I got this email back:\r\n\r\n[quote:286611e739]\r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: Roland \r\nTo: ph2t \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:41 PM\r\nSubject: Shhh, secret\r\n\r\n\r\nHehehe, Matt I think I might keep my cards close to my chest on this one for a little while yet.\r\nI only just got it all together today.\r\nI want to let the news get out there first, I\'m hoping to pick up a few mods out of this as well.\r\nAll will be revealed, but not straight away.\r\nSorry man, dont mean to be a prick, I\'d just like to get a little bit back from this one because I\'ve put a few hours into it to get to this point, and I am hoping to see some kind of return.\r\nCheers, \r\nRoland\r\n\r\n\r\n. \r\n----- Original Message ----- \r\nFrom: ph2t \r\nTo: Roland \r\nSent: Sunday, October 19, 2003 11:26 PM\r\nSubject: spill yer guts.....\r\n\r\n\r\nso how did you do the mod yer smart bugger?  c\'mon spill!\r\n\r\nDid you use another switching transistor?   Increase the voltage on the controller chip power rail?  ???\r\n\r\nthanks man,\r\n\r\nMatt.\r\n[/quote:286611e739]\r\n\r\nSo you can see he ain\'t gonna release this mod soon publicly.  bugger.   From a development point of view though I\'m happy to keep working with you to get a solution going.   This would be publicly available of course.  Your call man, I\'ve put the offer up but I need someone that has a zzse to do the goundwork with me, until I get mine of course, lol.   Tell me to bugger off and leave you alone otherwise.:)\r\n\r\ncheers Dave,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:286611e739]Hey man, thank for the heads up.\r\n\r\nYeah I didn\'t think he\'d spill the beans right off the bat. We\'ll have to work at him for some hints. \r\n\r\nI\'d love to help you in any way I can. I\'d love for this knowledge to be made public. No offense to micro_Amps, he\'s cool, and I don\'t mean to cut into his business in any way, but I think it\'s just way too expensive for us American pimps to send our cars to the other side of the world to be FET\'ed. I mean they are just toys, don\'t want to get too carried away. I like to keep a little levity on my obcessions.\r\n\r\nI saw that you were asking for some reading. I have a problem wih that. I have a cheap multi-meter, and for some reason it\'s range is up to 200mA, the it\'s next setting up is 1A. So I made a mistake buying that meter, I need one that reads up to 500 or 1000mA.\r\n\r\nSo I can\'t help you there, but if you have any crazy theories you want me to try out, I\'ll try to help as best as I can. :grin: \r\n\r\nHey you know my local Shack has the SE, if you need someone to score one for you, just let me know. I\'m tight on money these days, so you\'d have to pay up front, but you could use Paypal, you know, that way you could be an ass and take your money back, but I know you wouldn\'t do that.;)\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:286611e739]\r\n\r\nI\'m all for making stuff public and developing in the open, it\'s the best way to get some creative development.   The only thing that has stopped from doing a full blown tutorial style fet thread was that micro asked me to do it.   I\'m still in reservations mind you, but I\'ve met him and he\'s cool.\r\n\r\nAs to the readings they are for Voltage not current.  So check your mm for the voltage scales.  If you\'ve got a setting that is 0-10V full tilt then that would be fine :).\r\n\r\nThanks for the zzse offer, I may take you up on it one day.  For the moment though I\'ve got my brother nox sorting me out. \r\n\r\ncheers ph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12264, 'd43a27dee2', '[quote:d43a27dee2="VooDooMafia"][quote:d43a27dee2="ph2t"][quote:d43a27dee2="VooDooMafia"]Yo you are never on MSN hehe\r\n\r\n  hey you know the fet fix from micro amps?[/quote:d43a27dee2]\r\n\r\nhey man, yeah I\'ve been living at work the last week, massive network migrations, it sucks.\r\n\r\nDo you mean the zz se fet fix?  If so then no, he hasn\'t told me :(\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:d43a27dee2]\r\n\r\n  Yea I hear you about the work thing.  Even though I am off on perental leave I work more now at all my jobs :(\r\n\r\nAnd yea I did mean the SE thing.  I am not good with the electronic part of things but the more I read form you guys the more I learn :)[/quote:d43a27dee2]\r\n\r\nThat\'s cool dude, all the more for sharing.  Dave and I will hopefully figure it out ourselves soon :)\r\n\r\ncheers man,\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12271, 'ca23bd0dc9', 'Oh ok, I guess I didn\'t pay that close attention to your post, sorry man. I feel silly now. I guess I was just hung up on mAs. \r\n\r\nYeah I can get voltage readings. I\'ll be doing some modding tomorrow, I\'ll get to it then, and post my findings. \r\n\r\n...and yeah Nox will hook you up. I\'ve delt with him.\r\n\r\nI just didn\'t know if you needed a hook up or not since you\'re still waiting, but if you do I\'m always willing to help a pimp out.\r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12272, '71723fa154', '[quote:71723fa154="crazydave"]Oh ok, I guess I didn\'t pay that close attention to your post, sorry man. I feel silly now. I guess I was just hung up on mAs. \r\n\r\nYeah I can get voltage readings. I\'ll be doing some modding tomorrow, I\'ll get to it then, and post my findings. \r\n\r\n...and yeah Nox will hook you up. I\'ve delt with him.\r\n\r\nI just didn\'t know if you needed a hook up or not since you\'re still waiting, but if you do I\'m always willing to help a pimp out.\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:71723fa154]\r\n\r\nThat\'s cool man about the readings, no sweats, no biggie, lol.\r\n\r\n(sorry -VE means negative/ground, +VE mean the positive voltage rail, battery terminal, etc...GND means ground/negative, sorry dude, did a ee degree so I talk short techowise, :) )\r\n\r\nWith your MM put the -VE probe on the gnd rail or -ve battery terminal, if you can clip it there it makes taking readings easier.   Remove the motor from the circuit so the two terminals on the pcb aren\'t taking a load.\r\n\r\nWith no signal on the circuit, take the voltage reading from the two motor solder pads on the PCB, record these values in the table.\r\n\r\nNow put the controller at full throttle fwd, take the readings again for Voltage, record them.\r\n\r\nNow put the controller at full throttle in rev, again take the readings and record.\r\n\r\nThe reason to this methodical madness is to see what the voltage does on these pins.  If we can\'t increase the output signal from the chip (as micro states as being fixed at 0.9V) then we have to look at alternative ways of amplifying that signal.  The downfall of this investigation is that the end product might result in a seperate "piggy backed" circuit.  We\'ll see.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nmatt.');
