 micro_Amps, he\'s cool, and I don\'t mean to cut into his business in any way, but I think it\'s just way too expensive for us American pimps to send our cars to the other side of the world to be FET\'ed. I mean they are just toys, don\'t want to get too carried away. I like to keep a little levity on my obcessions.\r\n\r\nI saw that you were asking for some reading. I have a problem wih that. I have a cheap multi-meter, and for some reason it\'s range is up to 200mA, the it\'s next setting up is 1A. So I made a mistake buying that meter, I need one that reads up to 500 or 1000mA.\r\n\r\nSo I can\'t help you there, but if you have any crazy theories you want me to try out, I\'ll try to help as best as I can. :grin: \r\n\r\nHey you know my local Shack has the SE, if you need someone to score one for you, just let me know. I\'m tight on money these days, so you\'d have to pay up front, but you could use Paypal, you know, that way you could be an ass and take your money back, but I know you wouldn\'t do that.;)\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:286611e739]\r\n\r\nI\'m all for making stuff public and developing in the open, it\'s the best way to get some creative development.   The only thing that has stopped from doing a full blown tutorial style fet thread was that micro asked me to do it.   I\'m still in reservations mind you, but I\'ve met him and he\'s cool.\r\n\r\nAs to the readings they are for Voltage not current.  So check your mm for the voltage scales.  If you\'ve got a setting that is 0-10V full tilt then that would be fine :).\r\n\r\nThanks for the zzse offer, I may take you up on it one day.  For the moment though I\'ve got my brother nox sorting me out. \r\n\r\ncheers ph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12267, 'f3a0ef4797', '[quote:f3a0ef4797="VooDooMafia"]\r\n\r\n  Its all good I am sure there will be something down the road that will comeup or something.  At this rate I might be looking for alloy mounting lol, I have had this set for ages and keep fucking them up.\r\n\r\n  and  I will say this you never need to ask about a paint job.  There are only a few people that I would love to have paint jobs from.... I gots one already coming from CW and I personally think that you do the best paint jobs on that site(and ausmicro).  I dont visit to many other sites for anything other then looking for deals but I am sure you kick there asses to.[/quote:f3a0ef4797]Yeah, I\'d be down for a wheel mounting. After i get havoks out of he way, I\'m hoping to have it down to a routine.\r\n\r\n...and thanks for the comps on my paint jobs. Alot these guys around here have airbrushes, and I really think they could pull off something better if they\'d just try. Thay all begged me for the tutorial. After I gave it to them I expected to see everyone doing graphics, but I guess I do have a talent, since no one else is even trying.\r\n\r\nSo am I taking it you\'d like some flames on that there Beetle?\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12367, 'b86e733115', '[quote:b86e733115="crazydave"]Well I didn\'t get nothing else done yesterday, because I could wait to slap some flames on that Beetle.\r\n\r\nSo here it it is. I hope yo likes, because I think they came out perfect.\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=29882#29882\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:b86e733115]\r\n\r\n That rocks dude thanks :)\r\n\r\nand as for not getting anything else done thats fine by me I am in no real ruch for the cars back.  Oh nad just to let you know I dont need the box for the ultraman so you can toss it(prolly save a bit on shipping aswell).\r\n\r\n  I just made an order with bithed so I should have some more stuff soon and I found a guy in Hong Kong that is selling me some pullbacks (lambo\'s and AE86\'s) for 3.50 each so I should have a ton of new sheels to start some painting. \r\n\r\n  Hope you and ph2t come up with the solution on the se\'s\r\n\r\nPete');
