INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15823, '8484e5a0ea', '[quote:8484e5a0ea="CaboWabo"][quote:8484e5a0ea="crazydave"]I created an FTP account for you on my new host. You\'ll have to upload into the folder named \'bitpimps\'.  I also set up a subdomain, but that won\'t be working for a day or so.\r\n\r\nFTP Host address:  crazybydesign.net\r\nFTP Site username:  u35707516cabowabo\r\npassword:  cabowabo\r\n\r\nLet me know if you have any problems  8-) \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:8484e5a0ea]kick ass dude, thanks man!\r\n\r\nhey, what\'s the URL to the account (where the index.html was automatically created) under the cabowabo account?\r\nand do ya know if you can run PHP scripts on your server?[/quote:8484e5a0ea]Well my wife is incapable of giving a simple answer, so to the best of my understanding it is crazybydesign.net/bitbimps for now, until the sub-domain resolves in a couple days then it will be bitpimps.crazybydesign.net.\r\n\r\nDon\'t know if we can use PHP yet, my wife has just done basic html stuff with her free account, and I haven\'t had a chance to try yet, so I guess check it out and let us know.  :lol: \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15869, '02eceed782', '[quote:02eceed782="CaboWabo"]you know, I started thinking about it more - and do you think that\'s why the pimps aren\'t too interested in using it? cuz their gallery is almost hidden unless a user clicks to it?\r\n\r\nI\'m wondering if I shouldn\'t just snag their images (bitPimps guys) and post them in the "Custom Modifications" gallery?[/quote:02eceed782]Hmmm, well that could be, but if everyone would just get their galleries together, that section could be the major draw of the gallery. \r\n\r\nIt could also be making time for it. I\'ve been meaning to put together a couple galleries, but hadn\'t got to it until now. \r\n\r\nAnd you know also it takes a bit longer to upload the pics one by one. I\'m used to dragging the whole big chunk over in the FTP, but I think once they\'ve gotton all settled in, it should be convenient enough when just uploading a couple pics of the current ride.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12441, '78e443caf8', '[quote:78e443caf8="ph2t"]How\'s the car goin\' man?  OK still?  that battery problem hasn\'t raised it\'s ugly head again?\r\n\r\ncheers dude,\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:78e443caf8]so far so good.\r\nI haven\'t done a whole lot of playing yet, but will probably this weekend.\r\nI was kinda hoping to have body already built for it.\r\nI don\'t wanna run it too much without some protection lol\r\n\r\nwhat the paypal stuff, has steve paid up yet?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12442, 'd420c3b4ca', 'Im about to pick yours up today or tomorrow.\r\nse White rx7.\r\n\r\nabout this deal...I really don\'t need anything of your end.\r\nI was just doing the deal to help you out...figuring you could not get\r\nthis car.\r\n\r\nSo, how would  you like to just pay for what it costs me to buy and ship to you?\r\nI\'ll ship anyway you want...since your paying in the end...do you want insurance?\r\n\r\ntalk to me...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (13084, '92aeb8113f', 'Bloody hell Bruce, I sent a whole lot of copied \'previous\' emails to you using the hotmail address, and now you are saying that is down as well !!\r\nWe just cant win here.\r\nI got this as an email as well from the gte.net address, so they are still getting through to me, just not allowing me to respond.\r\nThe addresses I have been using all originate from dodo.com.au such as rolands@dodo.com.au and microamps@dodo.com.au\r\nSo the cars are on the way, good stuff, thanks. I will let you know when I receive them.\r\nLet me know how you go with this email stuff keep in touch and I will be happy to send test emails anytime you need them done so you can see if things are working.\r\nRegards,\r\nRoland\r\nJust so you know, this is a copy of what I receive when I send you an email.\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nThis message was created automatically by mail delivery software (Exim).\r\n\r\nA message that you sent could not be delivered to one or more of its\r\nrecipients. This is a permanent error. The following address(es) failed:\r\n\r\n  bdebde@gte.net\r\n    SMTP error from remote mailer after MAIL FROM:&lt;rolands@dodo.com.au&gt; SIZE=4223:\r\n    host relay.gte.net [206.46.170.12]: 550 You are not allowed to send mail:sc021.verizon.net\r\n\r\n------ This is a copy of the message, including all the headers. ------\r\n\r\nReturn-path: &lt;rolands@dodo.com.au&gt;\r\nReceived: from [203.194.51.29] (helo=c2i5w0)\r\nby relay01.kbs.net.au with smtp (Exim 3.36 #1)\r\nid 1AEQ3B-0000k5-00\r\nfor bdebde@gte.net; Tue, 28 Oct 2003 20:22:06 +1100\r\nMessage-ID: &lt;003601c39d35$a1422500$1d33c2cb@c2i5w0&gt;\r\nFrom: "Roland" &lt;rolands@dodo.com.au&gt;\r\nTo: "Bruce Ellis" &lt;bdebde@gte.net&gt;\r\nSubject: Fw: email problems?????\r\nDate: Tue, 28 Oct 2003 20:26:54 +1100\r\nMIME-Version: 1.0\r\nContent-Type: multipart/alternative;\r\nboundary="----=_NextPart_000_0033_01C39D91.D3D9F040"\r\nX-Priority: 3\r\nX-MSMail-Priority: Normal\r\nX-Mailer: Microsoft Outlook Express 6.00.2800.1106\r\nX-MIMEOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V6.00.2800.1106\r\n\r\nThis is a multi-part message in MIME format.\r\n\r\n------=_NextPart_000_0033_01C39D91.D3D9F040\r\nContent-Type: text/plain;\r\ncharset="Windows-1252"\r\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n.=20\r\n----- Original Message -----=20\r\nFrom: Roland=20\r\nTo: Bruce Ellis=20\r\nSent: Tuesday, October 28, 2003 8:04 PM\r\nSubject: email problems?????\r\n\r\n\r\nBruce,\r\nI am getting notifications from your email provider gte.net about emails =\r\nnot going through.\r\n\r\nIf you get this can you let me know please.\r\nI also am not able to view the vid you posted, but would love to orgnise =\r\nposting something like this on my website, with credit to you.\r\nAlso some news regarding my website too.\r\nPlease let me know if you receive this\r\nRoland\r\nP.S. Do you have MSN or Yahoo accounts? (I do but use them very =\r\ninfrequently) Maybe this might overcome the email problem. Id like to =\r\ndiscuss a few things.\r\nR');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12444, 'd7da316cca', '[quote:d7da316cca="SuperFly"][quote:d7da316cca="VooDooMafia"]Hey SuperFly whats goin on :)\r\n\r\n  Ijust thought I would PM you as I remember you telling someone that you would have traded then a clear body for thre race body.\r\n\r\nWell I got some cars in that came with race bodies and thought if you are interested thats cool cause I am just gonna paint them up anyway.\r\n\r\n  They are both skylines if you are semi or fully interested I can send yea some pics.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n\r\nVDM[/quote:d7da316cca]\r\n\r\nYeah, I\'m interested. The ones I already have are the Castrol (silver and black) and the Loctite (red and white), but I\'d be interested in the Calsonic, the Xanavi, or the other one I can\'t recall at the moment. Send pix if ya got \'em, or if it\'s one of the standard LXX or Bit-CharG just let me know which ones. I think I have at least 2 clear Skylines, and a white one and a black one.[/quote:d7da316cca]\r\n\r\n  OK here is a link to the bodies\r\n\r\n[url]http://www3.sympatico.ca/voodoomafia/race_bodies.JPG[/url]\r\n\r\n  If you are interested in these just let me know I dont care what bodies you wanna trade for.  To me they are all the same as I am just using them to pratice on my spray skills before I paint the nicer(super bit) bodies.\r\n\r\nPete (VDM)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12445, '9c977217d0', 'They are standard LXX bodies they just happen to come with the beetles I ordered.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12448, '923024e545', '[quote:923024e545="crazydave"]Hey been meaning to PM you haven\'t quite got around to it.\r\n\r\nJust to update you. I have all your cars mosfeted, I just have to install the alloys. I meant to get to the wheels yesterday, but VDM sent me his cars to work on, and I just had to lay some flames on the his sick green Beetle. (Of coarse he wasn\'t saying no). So you know me, when I\'m inspired, I gotta act on it.\r\n\r\nBut then lat night when I was finishing off the paint job, I suddenly realized where I went wrong with the Thunder Charger Mosfet mods, and had to test that out. Now I have to redo you Thunder Charger, Microspeed, and Yellow Mini. \r\n\r\nI\'m taking really alot longer than I intended. I gonna buckle down, and focus on getting your cars out this week.\r\n\r\nAlso been meaning to comment on a couple of your cars. \r\n\r\nThat Microsizer Impreza, what motor you got in there? \'Cause this thing is screaming after the FETs. Also I had to put the steering adjuster all the way to the right to get it to track straight, but then it kinda swerved back and forth. I discovered one of you rear wheels had come loose. So I crimped the axle, and glued it back on. It tracks dead straight now, with the steering adjuster dead center. With the combo of speed and handling, that is by far the most perfect car that you have sent.\r\n\r\nAlso, That Yellow Mini is pretty neato. Where did you score that from? I think I\'d like to try to find one of those.\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:923024e545]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHey, \r\nI understand that when you get inspired you gotta go for it......and I\'ve been having a really hard time adjusting to this daytime work schedule so I haven\'t had any time to play anyway....take your time...its all good.\r\n\r\nI honestly don\'t rmember whats in the MS Impreza...it might be a 4.2...what\'s the endbell color? and did I mark the motor with a marker? that will give me a better idea.....\r\n\r\n\r\nI know what you mean about that Mini.....I got it from Yagbols..I traded him a set of rims and some homies for it.....a great score I think....I know it only cost him about $15.00....ask him about it...tell him I told you about our deal and about all the stuff you\'re doing for me...since he lives in the Phillipines, its kinda hard for him to trust people ...you know?..tell him to talk to me about your honor..:lol:.....I will tell you this.....customs sucks big time....it took 5 weeks for me to get the Mini and 7 weeks for him to get the rims and homies....so if he helps you out...be very patient....\r\n\r\n lemme know brother.... :cool:');
