INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12482, '077ff12f7b', 'Hey what\'s up?\r\n\r\nI got your readings, sorry i didn\'t get them sooner, but when i was tracing wires I removed the battery to see where the black one went, and the battery in the SE is backwards, I forgot and out it back backwards. The car died, and I thought I killed it, because the battery still had voltage. Turnes out the battery was just pissed off, and needed time to stabilize. It works fine now, but I went and bought another SE just in case I kill this one. Also because I hear these Mustangs are improved. We\'ll see heaven\'t tried it yet.\r\n\r\nAnyways with the story out of the way. I came up with some interesting results. I have a better idea of hpw the proportional throttle works, but I have no idea what it means.\r\n\r\nOk, battery read 1.80v. There are 3 motor wires; yellow, grey, and black.\r\n\r\nWith the - terminal on the ground going into the board,the + on each wire at the motor\'s end, with no signal, read as follows:\r\nYellow 2.79v\r\nGrey 2.54\r\nBlack 2.79\r\n\r\nWith full throttle it did this\r\nYellow 0.00v\r\nGrey 2.54\r\nBlack 2.54 \r\n\r\nIn reverse it did the exact opposite.\r\n\r\nAs an added bonus I got some interesting fings when I had accidently reversed the battery.\r\n\r\nNo signal, battery reversed:\r\nYellow -0.94\r\nGrey -0.54\r\nBlack -0.94\r\n\r\nWith signal: well you know, the car died.\r\n\r\nSo I\'m not sure if that means anything either, but I thought it was interesting it was being limited to the range that micro_Amps said, but with the voltage reversed.\r\n\r\nWell I don\'t know if that helps, but I hope you find it interesting.\r\n\r\nLet me know what you want me to do next.  :grin: \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12483, 'f6c81b0b74', 'Hey man, thanks a heap!  Will analyse over the next 24.   Three wires to the motor?  bizzare.  Can you elaborate on that?  possible photo?\r\nAlso you said for the reverse it\'s the exact opposite?   I\'m sorry to sound dense but I\'m not sure what you mean?  in reverse yellow is 2.54? and black is zero?  sorry, it\'s harder to understand when it\'s three colours.\r\n\r\ncheers again!  speak to you soon\r\n\r\nMatt.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:f6c81b0b74="crazydave"]Hey what\'s up?\r\n\r\nI got your readings, sorry i didn\'t get them sooner, but when i was tracing wires I removed the battery to see where the black one went, and the battery in the SE is backwards, I forgot and out it back backwards. The car died, and I thought I killed it, because the battery still had voltage. Turnes out the battery was just pissed off, and needed time to stabilize. It works fine now, but I went and bought another SE just in case I kill this one. Also because I hear these Mustangs are improved. We\'ll see heaven\'t tried it yet.\r\n\r\nAnyways with the story out of the way. I came up with some interesting results. I have a better idea of hpw the proportional throttle works, but I have no idea what it means.\r\n\r\nOk, battery read 1.80v. There are 3 motor wires; yellow, grey, and black.\r\n\r\nWith the - terminal on the ground going into the board,the + on each wire at the motor\'s end, with no signal, read as follows:\r\nYellow 2.79v\r\nGrey 2.54\r\nBlack 2.79\r\n\r\nWith full throttle it did this\r\nYellow 0.00v\r\nGrey 2.54\r\nBlack 2.54 \r\n\r\nIn reverse it did the exact opposite.\r\n\r\nAs an added bonus I got some interesting fings when I had accidently reversed the battery.\r\n\r\nNo signal, battery reversed:\r\nYellow -0.94\r\nGrey -0.54\r\nBlack -0.94\r\n\r\nWith signal: well you know, the car died.\r\n\r\nSo I\'m not sure if that means anything either, but I thought it was interesting it was being limited to the range that micro_Amps said, but with the voltage reversed.\r\n\r\nWell I don\'t know if that helps, but I hope you find it interesting.\r\n\r\nLet me know what you want me to do next.  :grin: \r\n\r\ndave[/quote:f6c81b0b74]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (12484, '7ee9b56852', 'Hey man, had a chance to look at this stuff further.\r\n\r\nFirst, just to confirm your results, is this correct?  I just wanted to confirm what I said confused me in my previous PM about the results for reverse. So the Grey wire stays at 2.54V all the time?  Hmmm....\r\n\r\n[img:7ee9b56852]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/se_fet/results.jpg[/img:7ee9b56852]\r\n\r\nHere\'s the excel spreadsheet I\'m using, just update that. :)\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/se_fet/results.xls[/url]\r\n\r\n\r\nTasks:\r\n\r\n1) Could you take some readings again but this time for 50% throttle in fwd and rev please.  I just want to see if the Grey wire changes potential or not.  Don\'t worry about the readings you get at this level of throttle, just record and advise. :)\r\n\r\n2) Could you take some pics of the pcb from every angle you believe important.  Inlcuding the wires that go to the motor.  Also the chassis containing the battery.\r\n\r\n3) What batteries are in these cars?  Are their two or just one?  The 1.8V you describe is a wierd value.\r\n\r\nFor all these tasks I\'ve set you up an FTP account to upload the pics/data to.\r\n\r\nSite: ftp.prahranpianos.com\r\nusername: crazydave@prahranpia\r\npwd: bitpimps\r\n\r\nYes the username is that format with the domain choped off.\r\n\r\nOnce again thanks for this.  With what you have given me already I think it can be done.  I just need some more info to confirm things.\r\n\r\nThanks mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
