INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (13954, '5ea6f6a8d3', '[quote:5ea6f6a8d3="VooDooMafia"][quote:5ea6f6a8d3="SuperFly"]Thanks man! I\'m going to do your mosfet either sat or sun after thanksgiving, so I\'ll get that in the mail earlyt next week. Sorry for the delay on my end also. My good soldering iron is over at hue35\'s place, so I kinda have to do it when I have free time and he\'s home. 3 yr old has had a 104 degree temp for 4 days now, so no daycare = me taking care of her all day, working at night.[/quote:5ea6f6a8d3]\r\n\r\n  Its all good dude I am in no hurry, I just felt bad cause hue paid and I said it would go out last week.\r\n\r\n  Being a dad myself I can understand you there.  Only thing is when one gets sick they all do hehe.\r\n\r\n  Hope shes better soon :) and again no rush on the car dude get it done when you haave time.[/quote:5ea6f6a8d3]\r\n\r\nHey man-\r\n\r\nTurned out my daughter had pneumonia, pretty nasty. However, I did manage to get some soldering time in last night and got your mosfet Lancer put together. I also put in a custom matching antenna for you, and tested it well. Usually we just make sure the motor runs forward and reverse and that the RPMs sound like they should with a mosfet mod, but I went ahead and put all the wheels and tires on and drove it around for a charge. It was surprisingly fast for a stock motor. Anyway, just letting you know why there\'s a little dust on the tires. I\'ll mail it tomorrow.\r\n\r\nSuperFly');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (13955, '5ea6f6a8d3', '[quote:5ea6f6a8d3="VooDooMafia"][quote:5ea6f6a8d3="SuperFly"]Thanks man! I\'m going to do your mosfet either sat or sun after thanksgiving, so I\'ll get that in the mail earlyt next week. Sorry for the delay on my end also. My good soldering iron is over at hue35\'s place, so I kinda have to do it when I have free time and he\'s home. 3 yr old has had a 104 degree temp for 4 days now, so no daycare = me taking care of her all day, working at night.[/quote:5ea6f6a8d3]\r\n\r\n  Its all good dude I am in no hurry, I just felt bad cause hue paid and I said it would go out last week.\r\n\r\n  Being a dad myself I can understand you there.  Only thing is when one gets sick they all do hehe.\r\n\r\n  Hope shes better soon :) and again no rush on the car dude get it done when you haave time.[/quote:5ea6f6a8d3]\r\n\r\nHey man-\r\n\r\nTurned out my daughter had pneumonia, pretty nasty. However, I did manage to get some soldering time in last night and got your mosfet Lancer put together. I also put in a custom matching antenna for you, and tested it well. Usually we just make sure the motor runs forward and reverse and that the RPMs sound like they should with a mosfet mod, but I went ahead and put all the wheels and tires on and drove it around for a charge. It was surprisingly fast for a stock motor. Anyway, just letting you know why there\'s a little dust on the tires. I\'ll mail it tomorrow.\r\n\r\nSuperFly');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16108, 'ea768bd0ff', 'Yeah, man... I\'m in.\r\n\r\nSuperFly and I talked yesterday about this, and here\'s what we came up with... we, who donated the prizes, plus you for having the initial idea, will judge the contest. We figured it would be real simple if each of us ranked the cars from 1st to last and assigned a simple point system based on the number of entries (if 5 mods enter, then 1st place vote is worth 5 points, 2nd is worth 4 points, etc.) The first place winner would get to choose their prize first, second would choose second and so on... last place will get whats left. If all of the mods enter, we\'ll come up short... if that\'s the case, I\'ll donate a new-in-the-package Thunder Charger clone or 2, as needed.\r\n\r\nWe\'d like to keep the prizes a secret until they\'re all put together, but here\'s the list so far...\r\n\r\nCJ - Starsky and Hutch Torino ZZ SE\r\nph2t - probably a light kit\r\nbettyK - a suspension mod\r\nSessiz - a bitPimps poster\r\nSuperFly - a custom-painted, mosfetted car\r\nhue35 - a custom-painted, mosfetted car\r\n\r\nWe\'re not trying to take this thing over, but it may a good idea for SuperFly and I to help get the contest organized... we\'re good detail guys, and there are a lot of them to sort out here. You\'ll get full credit for the original idea, as well as putting it together with us. We\'ll definitely keep you in the loop at all stages, and you should let us know what your thoughts are along the way. The three of us is gonna whip up a badass contest for the head pimps... Is that cool with you?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (13957, '6f2fda2ea4', 'hehe dust is always good :)\r\n\r\n Yea I wish I had more time to play with the little basterds but with Xmas coming and with the Family deciding to come here theres been alot of work.\r\n\r\n  Only bonus is we still have not moved the stove from our other house to this one so we are using teh one it came with and its tiny (22 inches or so), so I wont have alot of cooking to do just lots of preparing.\r\n\r\n\r\n  I will let you know when it arrives, let me know on the MAts and pullback :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (13958, '1b791ac76d', 'hey man, did you get that package with the bodies and lights?   You should of got it by now.  Also I haven\'t got my efini rx7 shell yet, hope it gets here soon :)\r\n\r\nAlso, when were you going to paypal me the $25 bigones for the other order?  It\'s packaged up all ready to go but I got a few other shipments to make and I\'d rather get them all done in one hit.  If you don\'t want that stuff anymore that\'s cool as well.  Just let me know.\r\n\r\nThanks mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
