INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (14891, 'fc615590ea', 'hey man, good to see you around!   I read that you have a mini-z monster, what are they like?  Will you be doing any reviews on it per chance?  I\'m keen to know as I\'m currently saving up for a z but I\'m not sure between an overland or a monster.    If the bottom line is running over lawn, I take it the monster wouldn\'t have any problems with that type of terrain?   Also, where did you score it from?  The best place online I\'ve found them going for $139USD @ http://shopping.rcmodel.com.hk\r\n\r\nSorry for all the questions but I\'m keen to learn more.\r\n\r\n\r\nCheers mate,\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (14892, '966c260cd5', 'Yea I hear yea makes me feel like some Matrix shit when I have to see the code lol.\r\n\r\n\r\n    Ment to also ask if you ever did fet your xmod?  I saw some fets and shit for them on ebay but wondered what the performance diff was.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15492, '9685cf86f7', '[quote:9685cf86f7="crazydave"][quote:9685cf86f7="ph2t"][quote:9685cf86f7="crazydave"][quote:9685cf86f7="ph2t"]hey dude, love the pics of the 1/10 stuff.  cool as mate!\r\n\r\nI had a favour to ask ( yeah another one I know!).  Do yu have any ZZ chassis lying around? I just need the chassis. This would include the steering assembly and rear motor mount as well. I don\'t need the pcb, rear axle or motor(but id you can spare the axle and intermediate gear cog that would be sweet). I wanna do a tri cell monster and I hear you can fit 3 1/3AAA batteries in a zip chassis quite easily. \r\n\r\nIf you have it I\'ll happily pay you via paysluts or if that ain\'t an option I\'m sure we can figure something out!\r\n\r\ncheers mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:9685cf86f7]Well I don\'t have any extra chassis, but I have a couple extra complete Zip Zaps. I might be willing to sell one, as I want to get a Jeep, but don\'t want another Zip Zap, you know what I mean?\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:9685cf86f7]\r\n\r\nname your price brother.... payment via paypal acceptable?  my past experiece with USPS shows shipping to be approx $5 - $8USD.\r\n\r\ncheers and thanks man.\r\n\r\nmatt.[/quote:9685cf86f7]Ohh no, you said, "name your price". :roll:\r\n\r\nI\'m terrible with that stuff, so I\'ll just set it up for you.\r\n\r\nIt\'s basically a brand new car, only run twice. The only mod I\'ve done is the paint job. I really hate to ask you for the full 20 it cost, for a slightly used car, but I\'d hate to let it go for too little, since I have put a little work into it, you know what I mean?\r\n\r\nHere it is:\r\n[img:9685cf86f7]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/zz350.jpg[/img:9685cf86f7]\r\n\r\nMake an offer, and we\'ll go from there.\r\n\r\nBTW, a tri-cell Zip Zap is totally insane, but I think my dual cell FET modded cars are almost as fast. I\'ve yet to see what would happen with tri-cells, and FETs. Should be fun.  :lol: \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:9685cf86f7]\r\n\r\n$25 USD shipped.  How does that sound?   You can keep the shell if you want and just send me a regular shell.  How does that sound dude?\r\nI like the shell, don\'t get me wrong.  I hope I\'m not sounding disrespectfull.\r\n\r\nI want to doa tricell witha booster pcb.  hence the want for a longer chassis.\r\n\r\nlet me know if this price is OK with you man.\r\n\r\nthanks again brother,\r\n\r\nmatt.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (14894, '8f0c57cb7c', 'Thanks, Let\'s put it this way, I play with the Monster more than I ever had any of my other RC\'s including my EMAXX. And I run it thru the lawn all the time. About 75% of my play time is outdoors. I don\'t have an Overland yet, but many people over at minizracer have said that they like it a lot more than the Overland. The monster can go places the OL couldn\'t.\r\n\r\nI do know that the gearboxes are bigger on the Monster. I stuck an Xspeed motor in mine and it will out perform a fully hopped up Xmod. (That might not be saying much though.) It has a wide enough stance, that I can take turns at full speed and the tire grip good without flipping.\r\n\r\nI scored mine from minizracer, but they are out of stock right now. I like it so much, I\'m gonna get a second one to fully hop up with all alloy parts for show. ;)\r\n\r\nAs for posting a review, I wasn\'t sure Mini Z\'s were discussed on here, but if you would like, and check with Cabo, I can post something.\r\n\r\nThe only downside to the Monster is the lack of parts right now, because they just came out, and really ar not available in the US per say. So if you break something, you will have a hard time getting it running I guess. OL parts are different from the Monster parts except oil shocks, which I have. I have bashed mine pretty good, and nothing has broken yet. A couple of people have broken their damper mounts though.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (14895, 'bf46d11746', '[quote:bf46d11746="Ahh5hit"]Thanks, Let\'s put it this way, I play with the Monster more than I ever had any of my other RC\'s including my EMAXX. And I run it thru the lawn all the time. About 75% of my play time is outdoors. I don\'t have an Overland yet, but many people over at minizracer have said that they like it a lot more than the Overland. The monster can go places the OL couldn\'t.\r\n\r\nI do know that the gearboxes are bigger on the Monster. I stuck an Xspeed motor in mine and it will out perform a fully hopped up Xmod. (That might not be saying much though.) It has a wide enough stance, that I can take turns at full speed and the tire grip good without flipping.\r\n\r\nI scored mine from minizracer, but they are out of stock right now. I like it so much, I\'m gonna get a second one to fully hop up with all alloy parts for show. ;)\r\n\r\nAs for posting a review, I wasn\'t sure Mini Z\'s were discussed on here, but if you would like, and check with Cabo, I can post something.\r\n\r\nThe only downside to the Monster is the lack of parts right now, because they just came out, and really ar not available in the US per say. So if you break something, you will have a hard time getting it running I guess. OL parts are different from the Monster parts except oil shocks, which I have. I have bashed mine pretty good, and nothing has broken yet. A couple of people have broken their damper mounts though.[/quote:bf46d11746]\r\n\r\nthanks mate for that info, well detailed and it answerd several questions, I really appreciate it.\r\n\r\nI\'m currently going through the "get the most info I can" stage and deciding on where I wanna put my money down.  The monster looks like it\'s gonna be it.  So what\'s the lowdown on the electronics?  Can you upgrade the fets on these boards as well?  I hear that the electronics is similar to the overland?\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (14896, '41442b32d6', '[quote:41442b32d6="DarkTari"]A while ago I remember seeing a wheel mod where a disc of some sort was placed over the wheel spokes to give it a new look.  Was that you?  \r\nCan\'t quite remember. Not the "fill in the spoke" wheel mod you did.\r\n\r\nThanx![/quote:41442b32d6]\r\n\r\nsorry mate, I dunno about that one.  Yes I do know the "fill in the spoke" mod that you are talking about but not the first one you are reffering to.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nmatt.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (14898, '3a9c91dc29', 'ill dig up on MSN G! I got your X5 all set and ready to get out of the hobby shop. I figured they would ship it today or tomorrow, but since today is fucking windy and raining like shit docks, its probably tomorrow man. Its all good, i had a nice one. My MSN is Michaelchen135@msn.com\r\n\r\n\r\n          -Mike');
