INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15167, 'ec53138f25', 'Hey DT-\r\n\r\nHere\'s my address:\r\n\r\nGreg Maffei\r\n1906 NE Alameda\r\nPortland, Oregon 97212\r\n\r\nI\'m totally psyched! Ask hue35, I told him before the contest that if I was lucky enough to win, I wanted 3rd place. I liked your car the best of the prizes, and everything worked out groovy. Thanks again.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (17476, '6cb383094c', 'Hey, I\'m trying to keep my project for the mod contest under wraps, but I\'m getting excited, and have to share with someone. Havok donated the wheels so I\'ve been sharing with him, but he might not be around for a few days, so I\'m gonna clue you in, but since you are competition right now, I am gonna save the big surprise. ;)\r\n\r\nI was originally thinking funny car, but Ripper777 has already done one of those, so I wanted to do something a little more original. When I was a kid, my favorite class was always Pro Stock, because they were door slammers so they looked more like street cars, bad ass street cars that were the fastest class besides the funny cars.\r\n\r\nSo anyways, started with a pan car style chassis. Lighter and stiffer than stock. Made it from a Thunder Charger chassis, and Zip Zap packageing, so see, it is part Zip Zap, umm... by-product.\r\n[img:6cb383094c]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/prstkca1.jpg[/img:6cb383094c]\r\n\r\nI\'m proud of it, because it is nice and straight, and fits the ZZ chassis perfect.\r\n[img:6cb383094c]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/prstkca2.jpg[/img:6cb383094c]\r\n\r\nI made the front wheels from some Hot Wheels wheels. Had to dremel off the black "tire" part of the plastic, and I sanded back the front of the wheel, by almost half, until they were narrow enough for bit tires. Then I carved in a bevel on the front with my exacto knife. Painted the edge silver, and I think it nails the magnesium \'Mag\' wheel look. Used Motorworks tires to get that old school tall profile.\r\n\r\nThe rears are are made of some spare parts of alloys that Havok sent me when he asked me to mount his. I added a some dots to simulate bolts, and I think they\'re perfect. Used some tires left over from my alloys, because they have a taller profile.\r\n[img:6cb383094c]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/prstkca3.jpg[/img:6cb383094c]\r\n\r\nJust gotta wire it up, and do some detailing to make it look like an authentic early 70s pro stock car, but it won\'t be until next month until I can get paint and detail stuff. I don\'t want to leave people hanging, so until it\'s done, shhh.;)\r\n\r\nI seriously can not wait until this one is done. I rarely stretch these things out beyond a weekend ya know.\r\n\r\nDave\r\n\r\n\r\n***EDIT:Hey dude, I think I got busted for using my domain to swap MP3s. I have no access to my account. I had to move these pictures so you could see them. No big deal though, it was freebie account.\r\n\r\n********Double EDIT: I forgot you\'re hanging with Payaso this week...so much for instant gratification.  :lol: \r\n\r\nThat\'s cool, havok got back to me, and he\'s diggin\' it. So I\'ll just leave this here for when you get back. :grin:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15169, '53498e8d69', '[b:53498e8d69]One stipulation, you can\'t use it against me in a competition [/b:53498e8d69] :eek: LOL\r\n\r\nI really liked this one, it came out so smuth and perfect, the detailing and fade (my 1st) makes this peice very special.  Hope you enjoy it Pimp!  You\'ve earned it !');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15171, 'f8f06f73fc', 'Thank You :)\r\n\r\nBase was a crappy clone body. I lowered it by moving holes in the body. Cut holes with knife and dremel (lights, grills). Then i modified body with epoxy putty Milliput - grey/beige parts on photos below:\r\n\r\n[img:f8f06f73fc]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva//mrc/Foto1.jpg[/img:f8f06f73fc]\r\n[img:f8f06f73fc]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva//mrc/Foto2.jpg[/img:f8f06f73fc]\r\n\r\nNext was finishing the body with sandpaper. Lights was made of led diodes and plexiglass. Grills was made of photoetched net.\r\n\r\nI hope that this will help you.\r\nMiva');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15172, 'f53a0d072d', 'Thanx alot.\r\nI live on a small island and modeling stuff isn\'t readily available. But I can check the hardware store for epoxy putty. thanx for the pics and the quick reply.\r\n\r\n :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15173, 'f53a0d072d', 'Thanx alot.\r\nI live on a small island and modeling stuff isn\'t readily available. But I can check the hardware store for epoxy putty. thanx for the pics and the quick reply.\r\n\r\n :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15174, '409fc2306a', 'thanks for  the inspiration and not helping me wit the design of my track the blue print came out real nice its got 3 hair pin turns that get easyer as you go and the road ways are 8\'\' wide and  one of the hp turns is kinda like an overpass wiht a road way going up under neath it and it will be about 81\'\'x 30\'\' as soon as i hook the scanner up il send you pics  or attach them to my post\r\n\r\n\r\n[size=18:409fc2306a][/size:409fc2306a]\r\n :smile: THANKS A LOT  CABO!  :smile:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15493, '40c4752aba', '[quote:40c4752aba="ph2t"][quote:40c4752aba="crazydave"][quote:40c4752aba="ph2t"][quote:40c4752aba="crazydave"][quote:40c4752aba="ph2t"]hey dude, love the pics of the 1/10 stuff.  cool as mate!\r\n\r\nI had a favour to ask ( yeah another one I know!).  Do yu have any ZZ chassis lying around? I just need the chassis. This would include the steering assembly and rear motor mount as well. I don\'t need the pcb, rear axle or motor(but id you can spare the axle and intermediate gear cog that would be sweet). I wanna do a tri cell monster and I hear you can fit 3 1/3AAA batteries in a zip chassis quite easily. \r\n\r\nIf you have it I\'ll happily pay you via paysluts or if that ain\'t an option I\'m sure we can figure something out!\r\n\r\ncheers mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.[/quote:40c4752aba]Well I don\'t have any extra chassis, but I have a couple extra complete Zip Zaps. I might be willing to sell one, as I want to get a Jeep, but don\'t want another Zip Zap, you know what I mean?\r\n\r\ndave[/quote:40c4752aba]\r\n\r\nname your price brother.... payment via paypal acceptable?  my past experiece with USPS shows shipping to be approx $5 - $8USD.\r\n\r\ncheers and thanks man.\r\n\r\nmatt.[/quote:40c4752aba]Ohh no, you said, "name your price". :roll:\r\n\r\nI\'m terrible with that stuff, so I\'ll just set it up for you.\r\n\r\nIt\'s basically a brand new car, only run twice. The only mod I\'ve done is the paint job. I really hate to ask you for the full 20 it cost, for a slightly used car, but I\'d hate to let it go for too little, since I have put a little work into it, you know what I mean?\r\n\r\nHere it is:\r\n[img:40c4752aba]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/zz350.jpg[/img:40c4752aba]\r\n\r\nMake an offer, and we\'ll go from there.\r\n\r\nBTW, a tri-cell Zip Zap is totally insane, but I think my dual cell FET modded cars are almost as fast. I\'ve yet to see what would happen with tri-cells, and FETs. Should be fun.  :lol: \r\n\r\nDave[/quote:40c4752aba]\r\n\r\n$25 USD shipped.  How does that sound?   You can keep the shell if you want and just send me a regular shell.  How does that sound dude?\r\nI like the shell, don\'t get me wrong.  I hope I\'m not sounding disrespectfull.\r\n\r\nI want to doa tricell witha booster pcb.  hence the want for a longer chassis.\r\n\r\nlet me know if this price is OK with you man.\r\n\r\nthanks again brother,\r\n\r\nmatt.[/quote:40c4752aba]25 bucks shipped sounds like a deal. You can paypal me at davesmoejoe@yahoo.com. Friday and Saturady are busy days at work, so it will go out first thing Monday morning. Just get me the address before then.\r\n\r\nI want to keep the body, because honestly I wouldn\'t want you to judge the quality of my work by this paint job, it\'s not my best work.\r\n\r\nThese are the only 2 that are not cracked, or being currently used, so take your pick. I\'ll also throw in some muscle car hubcaps, because I have a bunch.\r\n\r\n[img:40c4752aba]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/zzbodies.jpg[/img:40c4752aba]\r\n\r\nCool?\r\n\r\n**Edit: Oh yeah, it has the stock 12:1 gears in it, and the Zip Zap 2.8 motor\r\nDave');
