INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15806, 'ac215b4237', 'The Big Boys were an Austin band right in there with The Dicks.... they did a shared LP together called Live at Rauls, Big Boys on one side, Dicks on the other. I go through regular phases where The Big Boys are "the best band ever". I\'ve made a couple of compilations... I\'ll send somethin\' \'music-like\' with the cars.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15807, '603d033cbb', 'all done and good to go mate.\r\n\r\nwhat I did:\r\n\r\nmosfet mod with clear epoxy for protection (pcb cover back on no sweats)\r\nguitar string antenna\r\nfront spring suspension\r\n150mah battery.\r\n\r\nShe screams.   Don\'t use anything below a 3.0 for this chassis.\r\n\r\nMy apologies for running this late.   This is a fully tested chassis, I tuned the suspension to make as equal turning circles on both sides as possible.   The mosfet mod has been soldered solidly and shouldn\'t give any issues.   The antenna is very flexible, see how I\'ve pkg\'d it as an example.   The 150mah is a must when drawing extra power using mosfets.   All the original parts are in the shipment.\r\n\r\nI just wanted to confirm your address before sending it out today....\r\n\r\nMr Glenn Sims\r\n7815 Quill Point Dr\r\nBowie, MA 20720\r\nUSA\r\n\r\nLet me know before I put the shipping label on it....\r\n\r\nCheers mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15808, '5e1360fe67', '[b:5e1360fe67]Glenn Sims \r\n7815 Quill Point Dr \r\nBowie, Md. 20720 \r\nUSA [/b:5e1360fe67]\r\n\r\n[b:5e1360fe67]Please[/b:5e1360fe67] don\'t put [b:5e1360fe67]MA[/b:5e1360fe67] as the state on it.  It\'ll end up in Maine somewhere.  I\'m in Maryland.\r\n\r\nHey man, I can\'t thank you enough for going the extra mile me a Pimp!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19051, '9b38a2b365', 'Hey man, I got da car today.\r\n\r\nIt kicks ass man. Excellent work. You did a great job lowering it, and that body looks so mean with the wheels tucked up into the wheel wells.\r\n\r\nIt\'s speed is precisely on track with my FET modded cars running Perfection 3.8s.\r\n\r\nThe handling took a little getting used to, as my little track I use most the time is all 90 degree turns with a couple hairpins. This cars steering radius was more than tight enough, but I think it\'s the springs that made the steering response sluggish. It threw my timing all off, but once I got used to turning a little sooner, I was making clean laps. That\'s when I realized I never made clean laps with my other cars sthat went that fast.\r\n\r\nSo now I\'ve decided I really need to redo my big track wide open for my faster cars.\r\n\r\n\r\n...and i could not find the idler gear for the Kit racer, I tore that package apart looking for it. You for shure if that was in there?\r\n\r\nWell any ways, thanks a bunch man. This is the best contest prize I\'ve won, and this will be part of the permanent collection for sure. \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15805, 'e9ac50006e', '[quote:e9ac50006e="hue35"]No problem, man. I\'ll grab the charging pads outta those 5 controllers.\r\n\r\nGrowin\' up down there, did you get a chance to see the Meat Puppets much, or the Big Boys or the Dicks?[/quote:e9ac50006e]I saw the Meat Puppets a couple times, met Chris Kirkwood at a party in Tempe once. It was mind boggling seeing them up on stage with Nirvana, in what would become the legendary last performance.\r\n\r\nI actually never heard of the Big Boys. The Dicks were from Texas, and although I never saw them live they did pass through Phoenix a few times. That\'s one of my favorite bands right there..."Mommy mommy mommy, take a look at your son. You might have loved me, but now I\'ve got a gun, and you better stay out of my way. I think I had a bad day. Mommy I think I had a bad day"\r\n\r\nGreatness.\r\n\r\nDave');
