INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16310, 'c20655c8db', '[quote:c20655c8db="midget_man1387"]Hey CJ. This guy over in Germany wants me to send him some parts for his XMod, but I\'m not sure what to get him. here is a copy of his e-mail he sent me:\r\n[quote:c20655c8db]\r\nFrom :  Don Helmudo &lt;Helmudo@gmx.de&gt; \r\nReply-To :  "Helmudo@gmx.de" &lt;Helmudo@gmx.de&gt; \r\nSent :  Wednesday, February 11, 2004 12:30 AM \r\nTo :  "\'midget_man1387@msn.com\'" &lt;midget_man1387@msn.com&gt; \r\nCC :  "\'michael.kohl@colt.de\'" &lt;michael.kohl@colt.de&gt; \r\nSubject :  XMod Printed Circuit board \r\n \r\n \r\nHi Midget Man,\r\n\r\nI?ve just seen Your Mini One XMod (on www.bit-racer.de: Realy great job and \r\nI like that car a lot.\r\nI also like my XMod and I will give it the a black AUDI TT Body from a LXX \r\nMini Z.\r\n\r\nBut before I do so, I need to fix an other problem of my XMod. After \r\nMircrosash gave it two aof the SI Fets a drove on Gym floor for 1 or 2 \r\nhours. There wasn?t much grip on that floor and the wheels were spinning \r\nall the time so the engine had to be at max almost constantly. Afterwards I \r\nnoticed the car had problems with receiving radio signals. The Problem \r\noccurs at 7m and more. The signal is getting lost for the blink of an eye \r\nonly, but makes driving on race tracks senseless.\r\n\r\nI have opened it last week-end to check the antenne cable and than I sa it: \r\nThe smal printed circuit board, on which the crysal is located, is \r\ncompletely black and plastik parts are in a slightly diffrent shape :-(\r\n\r\nSomeone from our forum posted a link some days ago with XMod spare parts:\r\nhttp://www.geocities.com/cjellis/rsuparts.html\r\n\r\nI don?t know what part I need exactly but I gues it is one of these:\r\n12414207 Y PCB ASSY RECEIVER $9.49\r\n12414215 Y SERVO ASSY $8.69\r\n\r\nWell, that means there?s hope. But as You know there is no RS in Europe and \r\nthey do not ship here.\r\nI am not the only one in our forum with that problem. Do You know a lot \r\npeople who own a XMod?\r\n\r\nMay I ask You for a big favour? Would You be so kind and check if there is \r\na way for You to get these boards?\r\nI gues e would need about 5 - 10 of these. I would take 2 or 3 myself \r\nbecause I do not know if the low grip driving caused it or if it will \r\nhappen again.\r\n\r\nThanks a lot for Your help in advance\r\nCheers\r\nDon Helmudo\r\n\r\nPS: please answer to the copied adress as well. It?s my email in the \r\ncompany and unfortunately I am spending a lot of time there instead of \r\nmodding my Bits (arround 25) and my "big" cars (Mini Z (LXX), XMod (White \r\nSupra that I bought on Ebay US ith everyupgrade)) and a Rocket Racer that I \r\nhave just received yesterday.\r\n[/quote:c20655c8db]\r\n\r\nso basically, what exactly does he need? \r\n\r\nthanks for the help in advance,\r\n~midget man~[/quote:c20655c8db]\r\n\r\n\r\nUnfortunately the reciever and servos are on back order for at least 6 weeks.  But the range problem can be fixed if you can solder you can replace L1 and L2 with 20% tolerance inducters:\r\n\r\nL1= 5.6uH DigiKey Part number - M7822-ND\r\nL2= 0.47uH DigiKey Part number - M7809-ND\r\n\r\nL1= 5.6uH Mouser Part Number - 434-22-5R6\r\nL2= 4.7uH Mouser Part Number - 434-22-R47\r\n\r\nL2 is not exactly the number which is 0.42uH but this one will work or you can search around for the same rating inductor.\r\n\r\nThese two topics may also help.\r\n\r\n[url]http://pub238.ezboard.com/fxmodrcfrm8.showMessage?topicID=324.topic[/url]\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=15683[/url]');
