INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16322, '6df0d4e0c0', '[quote:6df0d4e0c0="CaboWabo"]to be perfectly honest - you have every right in the world to post whatever you want about your SE fet mod.\r\n\r\nit\'s like anything with these little cars - most all of it has been done at one time or another - there\'s nothing wrong with writing something up yourself.[/quote:6df0d4e0c0]Yeah see, either he gives permission, and gets credit for his mod, or he says no, and don\'t get credit.\r\n\r\nHe\'s a smart guy, and played along.\r\n\r\nNow he gets credit for the mod, and micro_amps gets credit for doing something but no one know what. See how that works. ;)\r\n\r\nI love it when a plan comes together.  :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:6df0d4e0c0]many times people write how they talk to themselves, which is hard for others to understand...\r\nI\'ve seen at least 5 different tutorials on dual cells, each has their own pro\'s and con\'s in the writing.... get where I\'m coming from?[/quote:6df0d4e0c0]Is that the way it works? I thought those guys that wrote tutorials I didn\'t understand were dumbasses.  :???: \r\n\r\nI guess I\'m gonna have to rethink that point of view.  :lol: \r\n\r\ndave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15745, '0f630b354d', 'Dude,\r\nWhen I post, please do not put [i:0f630b354d]words in my mouth [/i:0f630b354d]by editing my post.  Everyone that read that post knew exactly what I meant without  wording it ! [b:0f630b354d]Let this be the last time [/b:0f630b354d]!\r\n\r\n[b:0f630b354d]Strike 1 ![/b:0f630b354d]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15746, 'd6ad107dc6', 'Hey man,\r\n your progress so far is great, and I\'m cool about waiting....I still have some designing to do on my track, working out the kinks...can you use any steering spring for the microspeed? I can take it out of pretty much anything I have. \r\n\r\nWork on those wheels, send some if you want, or send it all at once...I\'m cool wit it..\r\n\r\nI\'m going to send you the spring, and some other things we\'ve talked about. I\'ve got a couple of ZZ bodies for you to have and I still want you to check out that digi-pro for me. There will be no rush on that. I may even trade that if you want it.. I\'ll send these out monday or tuesday and I\'m sure I have your address, but give it again anyway... :lol: :smoking:\r\n\r\nI think I may be stepping up to at least 1 x-mod soon too...I\'ll let you know... :grin:\r\n\r\nI\'m glad I pushed you grasshoppa....and at an outstanding benefit to me...not just my mechanic, but my friend as well. you are very appreciated, by many more than me... \r\n\r\n:cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15747, 'cd46280c78', '[quote:cd46280c78="Havok"]Hey man,\r\n your progress so far is great, and I\'m cool about waiting....I still have some designing to do on my track, working out the kinks...can you use any steering spring for the microspeed? I can take it out of pretty much anything I have. \r\n\r\nWork on those wheels, send some if you want, or send it all at once...I\'m cool wit it..\r\n\r\nI\'m going to send you the spring, and some other things we\'ve talked about. I\'ve got a couple of ZZ bodies for you to have and I still want you to check out that digi-pro for me. There will be no rush on that. I may even trade that if you want it.. I\'ll send these out monday or tuesday and I\'m sure I have your address, but give it again anyway... :lol: :smoking:\r\n\r\nI think I may be stepping up to at least 1 x-mod soon too...I\'ll let you know... :grin:\r\n\r\nI\'m glad I pushed you grasshoppa....and at an outstanding benefit to me...not just my mechanic, but my friend as well. you are very appreciated, by many more than me... \r\n\r\n:cool:[/quote:cd46280c78]Well I have to tell ya, your lack of concern is part of the reason I\'m taking so long, if you\'d just say, "Hurry the fuck up", I\'d probably be done now.  :lol: \r\n\r\nSeriously though, I hate being rushed, and I appreciate the leeway. You did send me some challenging projects, and when I get frustrated I just have to set things aside for awhile, or I\'ll just screw it up worse, but I\'m sure you understand that.\r\n\r\n...and yeah, just a standard ol\' steering spring for the MicroSpeed. Those stupid little things are my worse enemy.\r\n\r\nSince you\'re not in a huge hurry, it would be better on the ol\' finances, if I wait \'til next week, when I get paid, to ship. If I put my mind to it, that should give me plenty of  time to finish up. So I\'m gonna make that my \'set in stone\' plan of the week.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe X-Mod is a really cool RC for 50 bucks. I can\'t figure out why Cabo, and payaso, are so resistant towards them, but I have to tell ya on the down side, 50 bucks just gets you in the door. Out of the box speed is not great, and you\'ll need to get the rechargable batteries almost right away. So after getting the car, batteries, stage 2 motors, and a tire set (the tires wear pretty fast on asphalt), I\'m already in the 100+ dollar range, and I\'m just barely on the verge of being satisfied with the speed.\r\n\r\nThe potential for hop-ups is unlimited, but it\'s just too much money for my budget. I want to get the bearing set before I do anything else, and that\'s what\'s holding me up, but once I get that out of the way, I\'m gonna FET mod it, so I can run Mini-Z modified motors. I already have a part number for FETs that are a direct swap with the stock ones, and the same ones they use in the Mini-Z FET mod. Then I might run a 5th or 6th cell...and TinyRC is already coming out with a CF chassis...and I still want the AWD kit and supspension set from RS...\r\n\r\n(Just so happens I\'m re-painting my X-mod at this moment, so I\'m kinda excited about, but I\'ve got no money for any of that stuff, so I\'m just day dreaming)\r\n\r\nSo anyways, go for the X-Mod, it\'s a lot of fun, but be ready to spend some money to get car that hoppin\'\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (15748, 'cd46280c78', '[quote:cd46280c78="Havok"]Hey man,\r\n your progress so far is great, and I\'m cool about waiting....I still have some designing to do on my track, working out the kinks...can you use any steering spring for the microspeed? I can take it out of pretty much anything I have. \r\n\r\nWork on those wheels, send some if you want, or send it all at once...I\'m cool wit it..\r\n\r\nI\'m going to send you the spring, and some other things we\'ve talked about. I\'ve got a couple of ZZ bodies for you to have and I still want you to check out that digi-pro for me. There will be no rush on that. I may even trade that if you want it.. I\'ll send these out monday or tuesday and I\'m sure I have your address, but give it again anyway... :lol: :smoking:\r\n\r\nI think I may be stepping up to at least 1 x-mod soon too...I\'ll let you know... :grin:\r\n\r\nI\'m glad I pushed you grasshoppa....and at an outstanding benefit to me...not just my mechanic, but my friend as well. you are very appreciated, by many more than me... \r\n\r\n:cool:[/quote:cd46280c78]Well I have to tell ya, your lack of concern is part of the reason I\'m taking so long, if you\'d just say, "Hurry the fuck up", I\'d probably be done now.  :lol: \r\n\r\nSeriously though, I hate being rushed, and I appreciate the leeway. You did send me some challenging projects, and when I get frustrated I just have to set things aside for awhile, or I\'ll just screw it up worse, but I\'m sure you understand that.\r\n\r\n...and yeah, just a standard ol\' steering spring for the MicroSpeed. Those stupid little things are my worse enemy.\r\n\r\nSince you\'re not in a huge hurry, it would be better on the ol\' finances, if I wait \'til next week, when I get paid, to ship. If I put my mind to it, that should give me plenty of  time to finish up. So I\'m gonna make that my \'set in stone\' plan of the week.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe X-Mod is a really cool RC for 50 bucks. I can\'t figure out why Cabo, and payaso, are so resistant towards them, but I have to tell ya on the down side, 50 bucks just gets you in the door. Out of the box speed is not great, and you\'ll need to get the rechargable batteries almost right away. So after getting the car, batteries, stage 2 motors, and a tire set (the tires wear pretty fast on asphalt), I\'m already in the 100+ dollar range, and I\'m just barely on the verge of being satisfied with the speed.\r\n\r\nThe potential for hop-ups is unlimited, but it\'s just too much money for my budget. I want to get the bearing set before I do anything else, and that\'s what\'s holding me up, but once I get that out of the way, I\'m gonna FET mod it, so I can run Mini-Z modified motors. I already have a part number for FETs that are a direct swap with the stock ones, and the same ones they use in the Mini-Z FET mod. Then I might run a 5th or 6th cell...and TinyRC is already coming out with a CF chassis...and I still want the AWD kit and supspension set from RS...\r\n\r\n(Just so happens I\'m re-painting my X-mod at this moment, so I\'m kinda excited about, but I\'ve got no money for any of that stuff, so I\'m just day dreaming)\r\n\r\nSo anyways, go for the X-Mod, it\'s a lot of fun, but be ready to spend some money to get car that hoppin\'\r\n\r\nDave');
