INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16229, '530ac11d04', '[quote:530ac11d04="CaboWabo"][quote:530ac11d04="crazydave"]Think that\'s exciting? I just tried CyborgZero\'s FET mod on the SE, and it worked. \r\n\r\nIt still not as exciting as a dual cell FET modded bit can be, but it is very cool, and I have a feeling you\'re gonna wanna be sending me that SE of yours, but not until I order more P-channels FETs. ;)\r\n\r\nI let you know when I\'m set to go with that.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:530ac11d04]son of a fuck! :eek: \r\nholy shit dude.\r\nnow I\'m like Son Gokou - I\'ll get all stupid and shit.\r\nI\'ve been waiting for this day, not only for myself but for the world.\r\ndude if you break this - and microAmps... (cuz now he\'s not the only one)\r\n\r\noh my god.\r\nyou little stoner, you\'re a fuckin genius.[/quote:530ac11d04]Shit man, I\'m no genius. CZ left the info over at TRC, and Son Gokou tipped us off. \r\n\r\nI was feeling sick as hell today, but I couldn\'t wait to try it.\r\n\r\nIt handled a Perfection 3.8 with the red Zip Zap gears, and it does reach appropriate speeds for that setup, and have power to spare, but there is still lag off the line compared to a FET modded bit. I\'m wondering how much of that has to do with weight, or maybe just the proportional throttle has to go through it\'s sweep before it hits full speed.\r\n\r\nWhatever, it works good enough, I\'m just curious if this the same mod micro_amps does.\r\n\r\nDave');
