INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19040, '0af2192132', 'hi hog i recently recieved an email from him and he is comunicating, he checks his mail at work and they have a spam blocker or something active on the systems so he did not get my pm\'s anyways he said he was sorry and was getting the 10 bucks for the lil rc and the shipping out to me as soon as he can, its all good right now, thanks for the atentivness, i am glad that i held out from posting anything until i gave it plenty of time, it had been two weeks since he received the rc and i finally got an email. i think its all good!\r\n\r\nthanks\r\njeff');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16494, 'a71a628315', 'Witam\r\n\r\nJasiu, jako gosc forum musisz zastosowac sie do zasad na nim panujacych. Jedna z nich jest obowiazujacy jezyk angielski. Dla wiekszosci uzytkownikiem posty w naszym jeszyku sa tylko zasmiecaniem.\r\n\r\nJezeli chcesz przekazac jakas wiadomosc do Petuma to wyslij mu ja w postaci prywatnej wiadomosci.\r\n\r\nJak chcesz obejrzyc zdjecia to na gorze masz przycisk Galleries.\r\n\r\nPozdrawiam');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16495, '1ab5c81d92', '[quote:1ab5c81d92="hue35"]No worries man, my address...\r\n\r\nMat Mathey\r\n3104 SE 39th Avenue\r\nPortland, OR  97202\r\n\r\nThat\'s cool on the comp... that kind of thing should just happen when it happens. I was gonna dupe a couple of Sham69 comps I have, but didn\'t get the time... I\'ll send those eventually, if your interested. I like the idea of an ongoing disc exchange... every now and then a new disc pops up in the mail... sweet!\r\n\r\n[quote:1ab5c81d92="crazydave"]Double BTW, I\'ve been meaning to ask you...are you a that Borg, Hue, that brought down the Borg collective by having a unique opinion? I been wondering about that for a while?[/quote:1ab5c81d92]\r\n\r\nNope... I didn\'t know about that Hue. I dig Star Trek, but I couldn\'t tell you a lick of trivia.\r\n\r\nThe hue35 name is a hodge podge of stuff... as a teen, I used to sign up for things, like the record club or Petitions, under the name Hugh Jorgan (Huge Organ). Occasionally, I would rope someone in to be my brother, Lar Jorgan (Large Organ) for double the fun. Anyway, when SuperFly and I used to go to the arcade,  10-11 years ago, my screen name was \'hue\', based on Hugh Jorgan... I liked the \'hue\' spelling and meaning in the video game context better. My dad raced Vettes when I was a kid, and his number was 35... so that\'s that. (more than you wanted to know!)[/quote:1ab5c81d92]I\'d definately be interested to here that stuf, That\'s right up my alley. I\'ve heard a bit about Sham69 before, and wanted to check them out, but never got around to it, you know how that is...\r\n\r\nAn on going CD exchange would be cool. Like Columbia House, but our music doesn\'t suck, and doen\'t cost too much. ;)\r\n\r\nI can\'t say I\'m not a little disappointed you\'r not the Borg Hue, but your story is prbably cooler.  :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI got the check in the mail this morning, and I\'m typeing this hurridly as i get ready to go catch the bus to the PO to pick up your package.\r\n\r\nYou know "Zooman" Got one from hime too, but i don\'t know who the hell that is. \r\n\r\nDave');
