INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16525, '3a3e21663f', '[quote:3a3e21663f="hue35"]Great story... the boy is hooked. I remember you saying that your wife didn\'t like little cars, but it sounds like she\'s outnumbered... you\'re officially a little car family.   :) [/quote:3a3e21663f]Good point. Thanks for pointing that out. The men will rise, and we will take over this household. :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:3a3e21663f]I\'m glad everything arrived... don\'t know what\'s up with the missing motor. All I can think is that once they were out of the package, I must have mixed one of my TCs in there... was it one of the yellow cars?[/quote:3a3e21663f]Why yes it was. That explains that. I thought it was a crazy defect.  :lol: Oh well, like I said, no biggie.\r\n\r\n[quote:3a3e21663f]Glad you dig the Big Boys cds... yeah, the Minutemen and Firehose are one of my all time faves. Mike Watt is one of my biggest bass infuences. [/quote:3a3e21663f]That\'s funny. I had a feeling you dug them.\r\n\r\n[quote:3a3e21663f]I\'ve never met a cd player that didn\'t play the black cds... does that player play other CD-Rs? I transfer a lot of vinyl to cd, so that\'s when I developed the look of the cds I make for folks... the goal was to make them look like little records, so the black discs were perfect. I won\'t send you the black discs in the future.[/quote:3a3e21663f]Well you know it is a boombox that I listen to in the bedroom. So it\'s kind of a cheap CD player, but it does play all my burned CDs. It does seem touchier with burned CDs than originals, but it doesn\'t even acknowledge the black ones. Too bad too, because I thought they looked really cool.\r\n\r\nYou\'re covers are the shit too. Very impressive looking. I liked how they looked like little album covers, but I didn\'t get the the black disc connection until you pointed it out. Very cool.\r\n\r\nI lost all my old vinyl about ten years ago when my cat knocked a flood lamp down while I was sleeping. It landed face down on the records, and after a while they caught fire, that\'s when I woke up, too late. It sucks too because I just never liked CDs as much as records. I used to have a nice BSR turntable with a good Shure cartridge in it. Damn apartment maintenence stold that out of my closet when I had it packed away. So I\'ve given up on vinyl. :roll:\r\n\r\n[quote:3a3e21663f]A sampler disc sounds perfect, man. No worries on how it looks, I\'m just interested in the tunes. I may not always do \'em up full-on because it takes a lot of time, but sometimes I just need to.  :grin: \r\n\r\nlater Dave,\r\n\r\nMat[/quote:3a3e21663f]Cool man, I\'ll let you know when I got something ready to send you. Probably start with a garage rock and a techno disc first. Those are the 2 styles I\'m listening to a lot of right now, trying to figure how the hell I can work them together.\r\n\r\n...and yeah I know it\'s fun making covers...wish my wife would let me do it.  :lol: \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (16526, '7b38b1f89d', 'Yo Pimp  :eek: \r\n\r\nGot my package a couple days ago and tore into it immediately.\r\n\r\nThanx for the extra goodies  :grin: \r\nAnd for returning the moola  8-) \r\n\r\nNow, this car is the shit man!  The stock motor does nothing in this thing but I slapped in a variety of motors and DAMN  :eek: \r\n\r\nIt handles great, speed is awsome and it\'s very controllable.  \r\n\r\nThe Guitar String Antenna is awsome, firm yet very flexable and damn near invisible ! I want to all my micro with this.  What do I need to get?\r\n\r\nNow to get an awsome body for this baby!\r\n\r\nThanx again Man  :cool:');
