INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (18471, '76a29c23c6', '[quote:76a29c23c6="Son_Gokou"]Ok, which FET is better than the other....IRF7389, or SI4562DY? You said that the 4562 isn\'t as better than the 7389 as thought...but it\'s still better, right? I mean, someone said that while it may have less amperage capability, it has lower resistance.....And that the IRF7389 has lower amperage capability, but it can handle that current continuously....\r\n\r\nSo, which is better and why?  :-( \r\n\r\nBTW I\'m back at MRCC, you may see me there as 100mph_Xmod.[/quote:76a29c23c6]\r\n\r\nMy testing has shown that the IRF7389 is better than the SI4562DY, period.   You get more torque from the IRF\'s than the SI\'s.   Even though people will say that the data shows the SI\'s to be better.  Real world tests show that the IRF\'s have a lesser resistance (Rds(on)) than the SI\'s.   This means that they can deliver more current to the motor.\r\n\r\nThe SI\'s can handle more current but that means squat in terms of performance.  IT\'s HOW much current the fets let though that determine performance.  Also, if you\'re stacking fets (which people do anyways) the less current handling by the IRF\'s isn\'t a problem anymore.......');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (17680, '2f369c69c7', 'No problem.  Just wanted to throw that back at you, for a reminder..  Its all good.');
