INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (18175, 'ea8744c24b', 'Hey, filelicker, I saw in a thread over on TinyRC that you wanted some info on the SuperSlicks, so here ya go... They are $20 at Toys R Us for a starter kit, 1/43 scale, available with a LOT of really nice bodies... They sell a "tuner kit" for $10 that comes with 2 hotter motors and gear sets, a neat little pinion remover tool, and some more tires and hubcaps(zipzap style, only bigger)... They just recently came out with a "quarter mile race kit" that comes with your choice of the 2fast 2furious Skyline or Mitsu EVO body, more tires and caps, and a SERIOUSLY fast motor and another set of gears to mess with for $10. They have a neat pistol-style transmitter which the grip removes from to double as the charger... The chassis is basically like a larger zipzap, only the steering has a gear system to smooth out the magnet set-up... and it has dual cells. The motors are longer and of a larger diameter than bit motors. Oh, and they sell body sets in packs of 2 for like $6. I have had mine since January and have accumulated both the tuner kit, the quarter mile kit, and a collection of like 8 bodies, all without putting out much money. The only thing I don\'t like about these is the TOTAL lack of suspension, and it is kinda loud. Oh, and only 2 freq\'s...27 and 49. \r\nI run the high RPM motor that came in the 1/4 mile kit with the stock low ratio gears, and it truly is a beast. Wicked acceleration.\r\n\r\nOh, the SuperSlick is the chassis that hogjowlz is using for the wide back end of his moderator contest project.\r\n\r\nThey are a fast, fun, reliable, and inexpensive car... I love to clear out my kitchen and scream around with mine.\r\n\r\nThey are a Toys R Us exclusive brand, so that\'s the only place that has \'em. Here\'s the site:\r\n\r\nhttp://www4.toysrus.com/superslicks/index.cfm\r\n\r\nI am seriously confused as to why these awesome little cars are not popular.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (18155, 'ad6c0084a1', 'I know you\'re busy with that testarossa (best bit body I have ever seen) and I am wondering if you know a common place I can find that wire mesh you used on your skyline...I\'m working on several new customs (although they won\'t compare to yours) a semi, an s2000, and not sure what do do with it yet, but a strange no-name rally-ish body.  Your ideas have inspired me and I want to go above and beyond what I would have done (first paint job), and I have studied up on technique.  I\'m sorry to have wasted your time, you must have dozens of pms a day.');
