INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19567, '38f8022b96', '[quote:38f8022b96="crazydave"]So what\'d ya think of that TKK? I never cared for these guys too much before so I\'m kinda curious how someone else thinks it compares to their other stuff.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:38f8022b96]s\'aight - way too much "house" for me to listen to on a regular basis.\r\nthis is their later stuff for sure.\r\nI was more into their industrial days.\r\n\r\nI don\'t totally trash the whole thing, there are a few tunes there with catchy beats, but overall - I just don\'t look at them that way and get the fealing their hanging on by trying to change their direction - and it didn\'t work. lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19569, '38f8022b96', '[quote:38f8022b96="crazydave"]So what\'d ya think of that TKK? I never cared for these guys too much before so I\'m kinda curious how someone else thinks it compares to their other stuff.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:38f8022b96]s\'aight - way too much "house" for me to listen to on a regular basis.\r\nthis is their later stuff for sure.\r\nI was more into their industrial days.\r\n\r\nI don\'t totally trash the whole thing, there are a few tunes there with catchy beats, but overall - I just don\'t look at them that way and get the fealing their hanging on by trying to change their direction - and it didn\'t work. lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19570, '5e72758c80', '[quote:5e72758c80="CaboWabo"][quote:5e72758c80="crazydave"]So what\'d ya think of that TKK? I never cared for these guys too much before so I\'m kinda curious how someone else thinks it compares to their other stuff.\r\n\r\nDave[/quote:5e72758c80]s\'aight - way too much "house" for me to listen to on a regular basis.\r\nthis is their later stuff for sure.\r\nI was more into their industrial days.\r\n\r\nI don\'t totally trash the whole thing, there are a few tunes there with catchy beats, but overall - I just don\'t look at them that way and get the fealing their hanging on by trying to change their direction - and it didn\'t work. lol[/quote:5e72758c80]See now that\'s interesting. That\'s kinda what I had the feeling people were thinking, but I think it\'s the "house" thing that has me digging this one.\r\n\r\nThis is one of those albums that just seems to go with baking out so well. It like it\'s start out rockin\' while while you clean out you\'re stuff. Then when your just starting to get baked out, "Hour of Zero" takes you back a notch. The "Flesh Playhouse" causes me to lose interest and space off. Then "Bettie" and "Heelz Afire" grab my interest back. Then by the time you get to "Asylum Disciple", it just kinda takes you into a zone to where your just sitting baked, zoning out after the album ends.\r\n\r\nThat\'s the way it works for me anyways.\r\n\r\nNow I wonder if you\'re gonna like the Ministry, that I didn\'t like. :???: \r\n\r\nDave');
