INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19606, 'c93c7d7ce1', '$9.00, I\'ll send cash !  I trust ya!  I\'ll get it out this weekend. :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19607, '30fe7583c6', 'I\'ve only heard a tiny little bit (like a couple tunes that were playing in the record store) of the Dwarves, but I dug it.\r\n\r\nAndre Williams is oooold school Detroit. He was makin\' records in the 50s through the 60s and burned out, drugged and boozed out. He made a comeback in the 90s, and had the Detroit garage scene backin\' him in various combinations. He\'s an old black dude that dresses like a pimp and is funny as hell. If you don\'t know this stuff, then I\'m definitely sendin\' some your way... two of his best records are on the same label as the Dirtbombs disc you sent me (and this is where I\'d heard their name before). "Silky" is engineered by Jim Diamond and Produced by Mick Collins, "The Black Godfather" has Mick Collins on it again, as well as the Jon Spencer Blues Explosion, the Compulsive Gamblers, the Cheater Slicks and the Countdowns.\r\n\r\nSo, yeah... it\'s all just a big cluster fuck in Detroit, apparently. I\'ve got all the Andre Williams, so I\'ll have to do up a special box set or somethin\' for ya... needless to say, it\'s way up yer alley... plus, it\'s laced with pimpness.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19200, 'e3c7663e8f', '[quote:e3c7663e8f="hue35"]Cool man, the feedback on that batch of discs will help me figure out what\'s next... I have a shitload of stuff and it\'s all over the map. Some things that come to mind are; the Nuggets box sets (vols 1 and 2), firehose, Mission of Burma, Wayne Kramer, Claw Hammer (this might be a big priority, if you\'re not familiar with these dudes), Link Wray, Captain Beefheart... you into Zappa? There\'s so much shit to listen to..lol.[/quote:e3c7663e8f]I\'ve got 2 CDs full of Nuggets that I got off of Napster. That is one of my all time favorite CDs, I love that stuff. I\'ve got the A-Z of Link Wray, another of my favorites. firehose, Mission of Burma, Wayne Kramer, Claw Hammer is all stuff that my buddies had, and I\'ve heard, but I haven\'t sat and listened to, like you do with your own music. I like Captain Beefheart, but I\'ve only heard a couple songs by him.\r\n\r\nFrank Zappa...I\'ll tell ya about Frank Zappa. I really want to like him. I\'ve tried to like him. I\'ve tried really hard to like him. I\'ve listened to Joe\'s Garage over and over, and every time I\'m left with the same feeling, like I\'m the only one who don\'t get the joke. It\'s a shame too, because everyone else seems to be so profoundly affected.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re digging on the White Stripes, then I think I\'ll send you more garage rock, as I\'ve got piles of that stuff. Ever heard the Deviants, Urinals, Swingin\' Neckbreakers, or Detroit Cobras?\r\n\r\nI\'ve got this one chick band, Bratmobile. They really kinda suck, but I love \'em just for the line, "Don\'t write a song about it, just give me back my Cheap Trick record" :lol: \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19201, '1ee57209a4', '[quote:1ee57209a4="crazydave"]Frank Zappa...I\'ll tell ya about Frank Zappa. I really want to like him. I\'ve tried to like him. I\'ve tried really hard to like him. I\'ve listened to Joe\'s Garage over and over, and every time I\'m left with the same feeling, like I\'m the only one who don\'t get the joke. It\'s a shame too, because everyone else seems to be so profoundly affected.[/quote:1ee57209a4]\r\nHave you heard any late 60\'s, early 70\'s Zappa? Hot Rats (\'69) and Over-Nite Sensation (\'73)? Those records are less "funny" and are the ones I was thinking you\'d dig. They have way more grit within the complexity and are a different thing altogether than the 80\'s stuff... the Joe\'s Garage era is so slick, that I would assume right off the bat, it ain\'t your bag.\r\n\r\n[quote:1ee57209a4="crazydave"]If you\'re digging on the White Stripes, then I think I\'ll send you more garage rock, as I\'ve got piles of that stuff. Ever heard the Deviants, Urinals, Swingin\' Neckbreakers, or Detroit Cobras?[/quote:1ee57209a4]\r\nThe only stuff I\'ve heard from that scene (if I\'m even close) is the Gories and the Compulsive Gamblers (via Andre Williams). I\'d love to hear that stuff... Detroit Cobras is a great name, I dig them already.\r\n\r\n[quote:1ee57209a4="crazydave"]I\'ve got this one chick band, Bratmobile. They really kinda suck, but I love \'em just for the line, "Don\'t write a song about it, just give me back my Cheap Trick record" :lol:[/quote:1ee57209a4]\r\n:lol: beautiful');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19202, '6920748433', '[quote:6920748433="DarkTari"]By the way the box is 10"x7"x6" and buldging so if your box is that large, it should fit!\r\n\r\nAlso you can do what you want with the bodies, paint the stock one or use something else, your call Pimp!  If you need bodies, let me know. If you want me to do a body for you to paint, holla  :eek:[/quote:6920748433]Well I\'ll tell ya, what I\'m thinking just based off my experience selling a few cars on ebay.\r\n\r\nIf we just FET mod, and paint a car, we aint gonna get what it\'s worth. I made the most money off a dual cell FET modded Zip Zap, that I didn\'t even paint.\r\n\r\nSo what I\'m thinking is, we really need to offer something really special to grab peoples attention. I\'m figuring I\'ve got a lot of attention from from my paint jobs, and everyone loves your body work...so if I lay a paint job on one of your bodies, that\'s gotta be a hit.\r\n\r\n...and since dual cell Zip Zaps sell for more on ebay, we got to stretch a chassis to fit a Zip Zap body. If I fetched $60 for a unpainted one, I figure one with one of your bodies on it should go through the roof. Maybe we can get Hog to build a charger for that one, and JB weld the rear end. \r\n\r\nI don\'t know, I don\'t have a clear plan of what I want to do. I\'m just trying to get on the same page as everyone else.\r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (19203, '8867f913db', 'We got one factor in our favor. Da Pimps know of our skliz and so do our US, German, Denmark &amp; Aussie counterparts. We are auctioning on BitPimps so I don\'t think we have to be too extreme.  I tellya, 80%-90% of our Pimps never go to eBay, I know I don\'t !  So I think we\'ll get a great response in Da Hood.  I would say do a couple of Extreme Micros, let me know what you need from me and it will be granted!   :cool:');
