INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20472, '48241e32bb', 'Yeah, I found the green gear to be just a little too extreme. Great top end speed, but I never had enough room to get there, and I would rather have the torque up front. Which is what you get with the red gear, even more so with the blue KIT racer gear. I almost never use stock orange gears anymore. Teal is usually my lowest, and the cars I race the most have blue and red KIT gears with mosfetted PCBs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20473, 'f6d1eb8d75', 'I\'m interested in a Whoa Nelly for my MR02. I think I want the 1.1, and I think hue35 wants one as well that can be shipped in the same package. How much were they? Do you have any available for delivery?\r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\n\r\nSuperFly');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20478, 'cd3b8676ea', '[quote:cd3b8676ea="ph2t"][quote:cd3b8676ea="SuperFly"]I\'m interested in a Whoa Nelly for my MR02. I think I want the 1.1, and I think hue35 wants one as well that can be shipped in the same package. How much were they? Do you have any available for delivery?\r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\n\r\nSuperFly[/quote:cd3b8676ea]\r\n\r\nhey mate, nelly 1.1 costs $25USD a pop, i can throw two into the same bag, shipping would be $5, 7-10 day airmail...\r\n\r\nI have two left out of my current batch that are halfway through production.  made the pcb\'s, put the mosfets on, yet to solder up the cables n shit.  I should have them done by the end of the w/e, ship \'em out early next week, no sweats...\r\n\r\nI\'m building the install doc currently, it\'s a fucken bitch, reminds me too much of my work doco, as you\'ll see when it\'s finished...\r\nbasically you solder the two fatass power wires to the batt +/- terminals, solder four wires onto the rx pcb.  the shit\'s color coded so you can\'t go wrong, lol..... \r\n\r\ndunno if you\'ve seen the latest developments man but check out the nelly thread at brucemicro, there\'s some pics of how she looks.....\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nfellow coffee freak..[/quote:cd3b8676ea]\r\n\r\nYeah I sifted through the goku shit in that thread. You\'ve really improved it from a slick package/low profile point of view. I have to admit I did have a hard time trying to figure out why one would choose the 1.0 vs. the 1.1, and still don\'t know. The installation seems like a piece of cake compared to mosfetting bit PCBs. Are there any issues you know of with an MR02 chassis, where your wires go into the PCB?\r\n\r\nSo I\'m gonna Paypal you $55 tomorrow for 2, shipped, right?\r\n\r\nBTW, did you want me to check into ordering you some fets from Digikey?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20479, '48241e32bb', 'Yeah, I found the green gear to be just a little too extreme. Great top end speed, but I never had enough room to get there, and I would rather have the torque up front. Which is what you get with the red gear, even more so with the blue KIT racer gear. I almost never use stock orange gears anymore. Teal is usually my lowest, and the cars I race the most have blue and red KIT gears with mosfetted PCBs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20480, 'ebecad3b68', '[quote:ebecad3b68="SuperFly"]Yeah, I found the green gear to be just a little too extreme. Great top end speed, but I never had enough room to get there, and I would rather have the torque up front. Which is what you get with the red gear, even more so with the blue KIT racer gear. I almost never use stock orange gears anymore. Teal is usually my lowest, and the cars I race the most have blue and red KIT gears with mosfetted PCBs.[/quote:ebecad3b68]Yeah that all makes sense. Orange gears are a bit too much with FETs. It\'s kinda hard to drive when it\'s pulling the front wheels off the ground all the time, that\'s why I was just half FETing cars for a while, but now I\'m running more cars with Teal gears, and I think that\'s ideal, but if I got hold of a set of those blue gears I bet I\'d think that was ideal. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo I\'m looking forward to trying the green gears. :smile: \r\n\r\nHave you tried stacking FETs? I recall ph2t running a car with some kind of ratio in the 3:1 range, with tristacked FETs, or his Biff turbo, or something, and it was kicking. \r\n\r\nI\'m figuring that\'s what I\'m gonna have to do to make the green gears useful, because this kinda reminds me of my original Bit Char-G trying to pull that pink endbell 3.8, back in the day. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20481, 'ebecad3b68', '[quote:ebecad3b68="SuperFly"]Yeah, I found the green gear to be just a little too extreme. Great top end speed, but I never had enough room to get there, and I would rather have the torque up front. Which is what you get with the red gear, even more so with the blue KIT racer gear. I almost never use stock orange gears anymore. Teal is usually my lowest, and the cars I race the most have blue and red KIT gears with mosfetted PCBs.[/quote:ebecad3b68]Yeah that all makes sense. Orange gears are a bit too much with FETs. It\'s kinda hard to drive when it\'s pulling the front wheels off the ground all the time, that\'s why I was just half FETing cars for a while, but now I\'m running more cars with Teal gears, and I think that\'s ideal, but if I got hold of a set of those blue gears I bet I\'d think that was ideal. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo I\'m looking forward to trying the green gears. :smile: \r\n\r\nHave you tried stacking FETs? I recall ph2t running a car with some kind of ratio in the 3:1 range, with tristacked FETs, or his Biff turbo, or something, and it was kicking. \r\n\r\nI\'m figuring that\'s what I\'m gonna have to do to make the green gears useful, because this kinda reminds me of my original Bit Char-G trying to pull that pink endbell 3.8, back in the day. :lol: \r\n\r\nDave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20482, '5091a19000', '[quote:5091a19000="SuperFly"][quote:5091a19000="ph2t"][quote:5091a19000="SuperFly"]I\'m interested in a Whoa Nelly for my MR02. I think I want the 1.1, and I think hue35 wants one as well that can be shipped in the same package. How much were they? Do you have any available for delivery?\r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\n\r\nSuperFly[/quote:5091a19000]\r\n\r\nhey mate, nelly 1.1 costs $25USD a pop, i can throw two into the same bag, shipping would be $5, 7-10 day airmail...\r\n\r\nI have two left out of my current batch that are halfway through production.  made the pcb\'s, put the mosfets on, yet to solder up the cables n shit.  I should have them done by the end of the w/e, ship \'em out early next week, no sweats...\r\n\r\nI\'m building the install doc currently, it\'s a fucken bitch, reminds me too much of my work doco, as you\'ll see when it\'s finished...\r\nbasically you solder the two fatass power wires to the batt +/- terminals, solder four wires onto the rx pcb.  the shit\'s color coded so you can\'t go wrong, lol..... \r\n\r\ndunno if you\'ve seen the latest developments man but check out the nelly thread at brucemicro, there\'s some pics of how she looks.....\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nfellow coffee freak..[/quote:5091a19000]\r\n\r\nYeah I sifted through the goku shit in that thread. You\'ve really improved it from a slick package/low profile point of view. I have to admit I did have a hard time trying to figure out why one would choose the 1.0 vs. the 1.1, and still don\'t know. The installation seems like a piece of cake compared to mosfetting bit PCBs. Are there any issues you know of with an MR02 chassis, where your wires go into the PCB?\r\n\r\nSo I\'m gonna Paypal you $55 tomorrow for 2, shipped, right?\r\n\r\nBTW, did you want me to check into ordering you some fets from Digikey?[/quote:5091a19000]\r\n\r\nhey man, paypal me the $55USD at ph2t@tpg.com.au, cheers....\r\n\r\nI\'ll catch up with you later, it\'s 2:19am here and I\'ve fuken tired....   more details shortly/.....\r\n\r\ncheers mate, \r\n\r\nmatt.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20483, '5091a19000', '[quote:5091a19000="SuperFly"][quote:5091a19000="ph2t"][quote:5091a19000="SuperFly"]I\'m interested in a Whoa Nelly for my MR02. I think I want the 1.1, and I think hue35 wants one as well that can be shipped in the same package. How much were they? Do you have any available for delivery?\r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\n\r\nSuperFly[/quote:5091a19000]\r\n\r\nhey mate, nelly 1.1 costs $25USD a pop, i can throw two into the same bag, shipping would be $5, 7-10 day airmail...\r\n\r\nI have two left out of my current batch that are halfway through production.  made the pcb\'s, put the mosfets on, yet to solder up the cables n shit.  I should have them done by the end of the w/e, ship \'em out early next week, no sweats...\r\n\r\nI\'m building the install doc currently, it\'s a fucken bitch, reminds me too much of my work doco, as you\'ll see when it\'s finished...\r\nbasically you solder the two fatass power wires to the batt +/- terminals, solder four wires onto the rx pcb.  the shit\'s color coded so you can\'t go wrong, lol..... \r\n\r\ndunno if you\'ve seen the latest developments man but check out the nelly thread at brucemicro, there\'s some pics of how she looks.....\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nfellow coffee freak..[/quote:5091a19000]\r\n\r\nYeah I sifted through the goku shit in that thread. You\'ve really improved it from a slick package/low profile point of view. I have to admit I did have a hard time trying to figure out why one would choose the 1.0 vs. the 1.1, and still don\'t know. The installation seems like a piece of cake compared to mosfetting bit PCBs. Are there any issues you know of with an MR02 chassis, where your wires go into the PCB?\r\n\r\nSo I\'m gonna Paypal you $55 tomorrow for 2, shipped, right?\r\n\r\nBTW, did you want me to check into ordering you some fets from Digikey?[/quote:5091a19000]\r\n\r\nhey man, paypal me the $55USD at ph2t@tpg.com.au, cheers....\r\n\r\nI\'ll catch up with you later, it\'s 2:19am here and I\'ve fuken tired....   more details shortly/.....\r\n\r\ncheers mate, \r\n\r\nmatt.');
