INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20492, 'bc66875606', '[quote:bc66875606="SuperFly"][quote:bc66875606="ph2t"][quote:bc66875606="SuperFly"]I\'m interested in a Whoa Nelly for my MR02. I think I want the 1.1, and I think hue35 wants one as well that can be shipped in the same package. How much were they? Do you have any available for delivery?\r\n\r\nThanks man,\r\n\r\nSuperFly[/quote:bc66875606]\r\n\r\nhey mate, nelly 1.1 costs $25USD a pop, i can throw two into the same bag, shipping would be $5, 7-10 day airmail...\r\n\r\nI have two left out of my current batch that are halfway through production.  made the pcb\'s, put the mosfets on, yet to solder up the cables n shit.  I should have them done by the end of the w/e, ship \'em out early next week, no sweats...\r\n\r\nI\'m building the install doc currently, it\'s a fucken bitch, reminds me too much of my work doco, as you\'ll see when it\'s finished...\r\nbasically you solder the two fatass power wires to the batt +/- terminals, solder four wires onto the rx pcb.  the shit\'s color coded so you can\'t go wrong, lol..... \r\n\r\ndunno if you\'ve seen the latest developments man but check out the nelly thread at brucemicro, there\'s some pics of how she looks.....\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nfellow coffee freak..[/quote:bc66875606]\r\n\r\nYeah I sifted through the goku shit in that thread. You\'ve really improved it from a slick package/low profile point of view. I have to admit I did have a hard time trying to figure out why one would choose the 1.0 vs. the 1.1, and still don\'t know. The installation seems like a piece of cake compared to mosfetting bit PCBs. Are there any issues you know of with an MR02 chassis, where your wires go into the PCB?\r\n\r\nSo I\'m gonna Paypal you $55 tomorrow for 2, shipped, right?\r\n\r\nBTW, did you want me to check into ordering you some fets from Digikey?[/quote:bc66875606]\r\n\r\nOk, had some sleep so I can now make a bit of sense.......   Basically nelly 1.0 is not as good as the 1.1  There is a slight cost difference, but not enough to make it feasible in a cost structure/marketing sense.  Nelly 1.2 will be totally different and will have a new pcb construction.  1.2 will cost more but when you see that it\'s approz equal to a 16x2 stack of fets, I believe the costs are reasonable....\r\n\r\nthanks for the offer of the digikey order Greg,  I appreciate that mate. I will prolly take you up on it at a later stage as I got a batch at the mo.  I will of course re-imburse you for your efforts....\r\n\r\nas for any particular issues with an mr02 chassis and the physical wiring I really wouldn\'t know I\'m sorry.  no-one in the local group has one.  shit I want one though.  I\'ve gone through my fucken 7th first servo gear and I\'m sick of busting it!  the mr02 has the servo saver spring system on the front servo gearbox which would save $$ in the long run.....\r\nthe pcb is the same in the madforce and mr02, they both have the brake function.  from the photo\'s I\'ve seen on the net though man the layout is the same.  I\'ve got pics for the mini-z and iwaver and CJ helpout last night and got me a pic for the xmod PCB.\r\n\r\nCheers dude,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
