INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20789, 'd6d4073195', 'I got it.  I had the wrong letter.  I mistaken the "G" as in Gold, for "Q" as in Queen.  I resent it.\r\n\r\nPayPal just takes the $$$ back and it doesn\'t go anywhere, but to and from nowhere.  It\'s cool.  My mistake.\r\n\r\nIt should be wigglin\' down the pipeline now.\r\n\r\nThanks, \r\n\r\n\r\nMike');
INSERT INTO phpbb_privmsgs_text VALUES (20960, 'f5ced23e49', '[quote:f5ced23e49="SuperFly"][quote:f5ced23e49="ph2t"]hey man,  I wanted to take you up on that offer of scoring shit from digikey.  The way I see it is that I order the stuff online but put your shipping details in there.\r\n\r\nare you ok with this?\r\n\r\nOR: would you rather I just paypal you the total and you order from digikey with a parts list prepared by me?\r\n\r\nI think the first scenario would be better, less work on your part.\r\n\r\nCheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:f5ced23e49]\r\n\r\nNo problem, Matt. Your suggestion sounds great, that way I can\'t fuck it up and get the wrong thing. While we\'re at it, I think I might want to add some bit FETs to the order, since they have that minimum order charge and I don\'t need that many. Can we add 50 fets for bits to the order? You have the part number for those, I assume. \r\n\r\nHere\'s the address you should use for shipping:\r\n\r\nGreg Maffei\r\nGrey Matter\r\n431 NW Flanders, #203\r\nPortland, Oregon 97209  \r\n\r\nIt\'s my office address, so they won\'t be sitting on my porch all day. I can probably re-ship them the same day they arrive here, the post office is 5 blocks away from my office. There\'s a possibility I can Fed-Ex them you you on one of my client\'s dimes.\r\n\r\nAlso, about the Whoa Nellys... Sorry for being flakey about ordering those. Hue35 and I are definitely interested in going that route, however, we are feeling like we need to figure out our track surface and racing situation first. As it is, we are at the limits of traction/handling with a non-turbo motor like X-speed. We\'re thinking about getting one of those RCP tracks, but for the size we\'re accustomed to racing on, we\'ll need to drop $400 on it. I\'ll keep you posted....\r\n\r\nAlso, I saw you asking in some thread about MR01 vs. MR02 handling. Hue35 and I are running both kinds, and I can give you my opinions as needed. Out of the box, the MR02 is vastly superior. It weighs much less, and the weight is all lower, making for a more precise and quicker car. Kinda feels like driving a Porsche, where it\'s not so much about controlled sliding as it is just pointing it where you want to go and it will track. With the MR01, it feels more like driving a muscle car where you have to throw the weight around more, control your slippage, and it could flip if you have enough grip. \r\n\r\nThat\'s it for now,\r\nGreg[/quote:f5ced23e49]\r\n\r\nthanks for the info greg, I take it you want 50 IRMLM2502 mosfets? no problems, I\'ll add them to the order.  you can set me up later for \'em.\r\n\r\nlol, a bit resourcefull hey?  fedex on a client\'s account, I love it! haha....  again, hit me for the shipping when it all happens.\r\n\r\nas for nelly, that\'s cool.  I\'m running out of mosfets quicker than I expected so that\'s why the order is happening.\r\n\r\nI\'d love to get an mr02, but I\'ve invested mega moola in the mr01.....\r\n\r\nI\'ll let you know when the order is done.  What postal option do you reccomend?\r\n\r\nthanks again mate,\r\n\r\nMatt.');
